        injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch HFM (Hot-Film Mass Air Flow). Unlike the disastrous PMS systems, this utilizes a reliable Hot-Film Mass Air Flow sensor to accurately measure the compressed air. The fuel injectors are significantly larger to supply the necessary fuel under supercharged boost. This early forced-induction system is robust but sensitive to PCV oil contamination.)",
        engineLifespan: "350,000 - 450,000+ km (The mechanical core of the M111 is a heavy cast-iron block with forged internals. Mercedes engineered this block to handle massive cylinder pressures, meaning the factory 193hp output leaves the engine entirely unstressed. The true lifespan limiter is the Eaton M62 supercharger itself, which requires specific oil changes to its internal planetary gears that are almost universally ignored by owners.)",
        turboType: "Supercharged (Equipped with an Eaton M62 Roots-type positive displacement supercharger. Driven directly by the engine's serpentine belt via an electromagnetic clutch. It provides massive, instantaneous boost the second the throttle is pressed, completely eliminating lag. The magnetic clutch engages the supercharger only under load with a distinct 'clack' sound.)",
        ecuType: "Bosch HFM (A highly sophisticated and reliable engine management system for its era. It meticulously controls fuel injection, ignition, and the engagement of the supercharger's magnetic clutch. While not as easily flashable as later ME systems, it can be chipped to accommodate smaller supercharger pulleys for power gains.)",
