        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM604 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine producing very low torque, this timing system is massively over-engineered. It is a true 'lifetime' component that will effortlessly exceed 500 000 kilometers without stretching, provided basic 10 000 km oil changes are performed.)",
        injectionType: "Indirect Injection / Lucas EPIC (Pre-chamber injection. Here lies the absolute Achilles heel of this engine. Instead of using the legendary mechanical Bosch inline pumps found in earlier Mercedes diesels, the OM604 uses a Lucas EPIC (Electronically Programmed Injection Control) distributor pump. This early attempt at electronic diesel injection is globally infamous for its catastrophic failure rate. The internal rubber seals harden, and the pump leaks diesel profusely onto the engine block and directly into its own wiring harness.)",
        engineLifespan: "400 000+ km (The iron block and the sophisticated 16-valve aluminum cylinder head are exceptionally durable, capable of running forever. However, the economic lifespan of the vehicle is entirely dictated by the disastrous Lucas injection pump. Once the pump fails or leaks, the cost to rebuild it often exceeds the value of the entire car. The only permanent fix is retrofitting a mechanical Bosch pump from an older OM601.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The OM604 relies entirely on massive 22.0:1 compression and its 16-valve breathing capability to generate 150 Nm of torque. Power delivery is extremely lethargic, making highway merging a highly calculated endeavor, though it is incredibly smooth and linear.)",
        ecuType: "Lucas EPIC Controller (A highly vulnerable electronic control unit managing the notoriously unreliable Lucas injection pump. It relies on a multitude of internal pump sensors for rotor position and fuel temperature. When the pump leaks internally, diesel fuel is pushed through the wiring harness directly into the ECU via capillary action, permanently destroying the computer.)",
        euroStandard: "Euro 1 / Euro 2",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "150+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block is indestructible. However, tuning the Lucas EPIC system natively is completely impossible. Achieving any power requires throwing the entire Lucas system in the garbage, fabricating an exhaust manifold, bolting on a turbocharger, and installing a mechanical Bosch injection pump built with larger elements.)",
