        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM605 utilizes a massively overbuilt duplex (double-row) timing chain. Despite the immense torque of the turbocharger, this timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component that will effortlessly exceed 500 000 kilometers without stretching, provided basic 10 000 kilometer oil changes are performed faithfully.)",
        injectionType: "Indirect Injection / Bosch ERE (Pre-chamber injection. Uses the Bosch ERE electronically controlled inline injection pump. It utilizes an electronic actuator to govern fuel delivery based on boost pressure, offering excellent performance and reliability. However, this relies on the EDC module and the engine wiring harness, making it vulnerable to electrical shorts on early models.)",
        engineLifespan: "500 000+ km (The iron block, forged internals, and the sophisticated 20-valve aluminum cylinder head are exceptionally durable, capable of running forever. The turbocharged OM605 is globally renowned as one of the toughest engines ever built. The economic lifespan of the vehicle is entirely dictated by the structural rust of the W202 chassis and the potential failure of the biodegradable wiring harness on pre-1997 models.)",
        turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a wastegate turbocharger, typically a Garrett or KKK unit. It provides 280 Nm of torque, transforming the lethargic naturally aspirated engine into a genuinely fast and highly capable highway cruiser. The turbo is cooled by oil and is incredibly reliable if allowed to cool down after hard driving.)",
        ecuType: "Bosch EDC (Electronic Diesel Control module manages the Bosch ERE injection pump. The EDC strictly monitors boost pressure, fuel delivery, and transmission shifts. If the biodegradable engine wiring harness crumbles and shorts out, it will permanently destroy this expensive control unit.)",
        euroStandard: "Euro 2",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block and forged internal rotating assembly are utterly indestructible. This engine is a legend in the tuning community. Achieving massive power requires completely removing the electronic ERE pump, installing a fully mechanical Bosch pump built with 7.5mm elements, and fitting a massive Holset turbocharger. The stock bottom end handles 2.0+ bar of boost effortlessly.)",
