        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M271 utilizes a highly controversial and disastrous single-row (simplex) timing chain, a massive downgrade from earlier engines. This single-row chain is incredibly prone to stretching prematurely due to the stress of the variable valve timing system. When the chain stretches, it rapidly machines and destroys the teeth on the incredibly expensive VVT camshaft gears. If the cold-start rattle is ignored, the chain will skip teeth, causing catastrophic piston-to-valve contact. It MUST be replaced preventatively every 100 000 kilometers along with the tensioner.)",
        injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Siemens SIM4 LKE (A highly advanced sequential electronic fuel injection system. It utilizes a highly sensitive Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor. The most notorious issue is the camshaft adjuster magnets leaking engine oil directly into the engine wiring harness. Through capillary action, this oil travels all the way into the Siemens ECU, destroying the entire electronic injection control system if isolation pigtails are not installed.)",
        engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M271 engine block is entirely dictated by the owner's vigilance regarding the timing chain. If the timing chain and camshaft gears are replaced exactly when needed, the engine bottom end will last a very long time. Because this specific variant is artificially restricted to 122 horsepower for tax purposes, the internal rotating assembly is completely unstressed. The vehicle's ultimate demise is almost always caused by neglected timing chains snapping or ECU flooding.)",
        turboType: "Supercharged (Equipped with a continuously driven Eaton M45 Roots-type positive displacement supercharger. Unlike older M111 engines, this supercharger does not have an electromagnetic clutch; it spins constantly with the engine, providing absolutely seamless throttle response. However, because it spins constantly, the internal planetary gears wear out much faster. The specialized aviation oil inside the supercharger snout must be changed every 100 000 kilometers to prevent bearing seizure.)",
        ecuType: "Siemens SIM4 LKE (A highly complex engine management system. This specific ECU is mapped with a severe, artificial restriction, limiting the engine to exactly 122 horsepower to slip under strict Belgian and Dutch tax brackets. The ECU is incredibly vulnerable to oil intrusion from the engine wiring harness. If oil reaches the ECU pins, the entire unit will short out and require replacement. Because it is artificially restricted, it is highly tunable.)",
        euroStandard: "Euro 4",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "250+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 1.8-liter M271 is robust enough to handle significantly more power than the artificially limited 122 horsepower factory rating. Because this engine is physically identical to the 192 horsepower variant, the stock internals are vastly overbuilt for this specific application. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the Eaton M45 supercharger, which superheats the intake air if spun too fast.)",
