        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M112 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain that represents the absolute zenith of Mercedes-Benz engineering before the cost-cutting era. Unlike the disastrous single-row chains found in the 4-cylinder models, this heavy-duty timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component. The massive steel chain glides on highly reinforced polymer guide rails and is kept under optimal, constant tension by a hydraulic tensioner. If the owner strictly adheres to 10 000 kilometer oil change intervals using high-quality synthetic lubricants, this timing chain assembly will rarely require servicing before 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers.)",
        injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 2.8 (This engine features a fully electronic, highly advanced sequential fuel injection system managed by the highly robust Bosch ME architecture. It utilizes a highly accurate Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor to measure incoming air. This specific North American variant incorporates stringent OBD-II diagnostic software to meticulously monitor catalytic converter efficiency via multiple oxygen sensors. The injection system itself is incredibly reliable and virtually never suffers from the capillary oil wicking issues that destroy the computers on later models.)",
        engineLifespan: "400 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the M112 is a massive, heavily reinforced aluminum engine block with Silitec liners that is globally legendary for its near-indestructible durability. Because this specific US C 240 variant utilizes a 2.6-liter displacement to produce a highly conservative 168 horsepower, the physical engine components are almost completely unstressed. Wear on the cylinder walls and bearings is virtually nonexistent even after decades of heavy use. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W203 chassis that surrounds it, provided the harmonic balancer is monitored.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (The engine relies entirely on atmospheric pressure, completely lacking any turbocharger or supercharger. Instead of forced induction, Mercedes-Benz engineers focused on optimizing the cylinder head flow to provide a beautifully smooth, linear torque curve. The power delivery is exceptionally refined and entirely devoid of the sudden surges or lags associated with forced induction. It prioritizes absolute smoothness, quiet operation, and relaxed waftability on American highways over aggressive, sudden acceleration.)",
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.8 (A highly sophisticated and incredibly reliable electronic engine control module that serves as the absolute mastermind of the powertrain. It flawlessly coordinates fuel pressure monitoring, electronic throttle actuation, and complex immobilizer security protocols. This specific ECU features a highly sensitive mapping for US emissions compliance. Because this engine is heavily over-engineered, the Bosch ECU rarely fails unless subjected to severe water intrusion from blocked cowl drains near the windshield.)",
        euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 2 / OBD-II Compliant",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The aluminum block, robust cooling jackets, and forged internal rotating assembly of the 2.6L M112 are vastly overbuilt for the factory 168 horsepower output. The absolute limiting factor for producing massive horsepower is the naturally aspirated induction system. The bottom end can easily, reliably handle forced induction. However, installing a supercharger on a 2.6L C 240 is financially illogical when the identical 3.2L M112 or the 5.0L M113 V8 bolts right into the same engine bay.)",
