    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 utilizes a double-row timing chain. However, early production engines are globally infamous for a catastrophic flaw: the balance shaft chain sprocket was manufactured with insufficiently hardened steel. This gear wears down prematurely, throwing off engine timing and triggering P0016/P0017 codes. Repairing this requires completely removing the engine and tearing down the block. This was resolved on later serial numbers, but early models are highly dangerous.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system mapped specifically for extremely strict US SULEV emissions. It utilizes modern electronic throttle control and a highly sensitive Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor. The system is extremely reliable and completely avoids the capillary oil wicking issues that plagued the 4-cylinder engines. However, the intake manifold features variable-length runners controlled by plastic swirl flap arms that frequently break and trigger severe performance issues.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 400 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M272 V6 engine block is completely bifurcated. If the engine falls into the defective balance shaft serial number range and the repair has not been done, the engine will self-destruct prematurely. If the engine has the updated hardened balance shaft gear, or falls outside the defective range, it is an incredibly robust, deeply refined V6 that will easily outlast the W203 chassis with basic maintenance.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 relies entirely on its larger 3.0-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate its incredibly smooth power delivery. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids the complex supercharger maintenance issues of the Kompressor models, making the engine bay significantly simpler.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system designed to tightly control strict American SULEV emissions and precisely manage the continuously variable valve timing. The ECU actively monitors the catalytic converters with extreme sensitivity. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine mapped close to its natural efficiency limits, tuning potential is practically nonexistent, making the ECU a 'leave it alone' component.)",
