    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block on some OM642 variants, but traditionally front-driven on the W203 setup. The OM642 utilizes a simplex (single-row) timing chain. While significantly more durable than the catastrophic gasoline M271 chains, it is known to stretch over high mileages (250 000+ km). When it stretches, it causes timing correlation errors and a distinct cold-start rattle. Replacing it is highly labor-intensive due to the V6 packaging in the compact W203 engine bay.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC16CP31 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 3 Common Rail system operating at 1 600 bar via a Bosch CP3 pump. It utilizes lightning-fast piezo injectors capable of multiple precisely timed injections per stroke. This entirely eradicates traditional diesel clatter, making the V6 sound incredibly smooth and refined. However, these piezo injectors are extremely sensitive to poor fuel quality and are astronomically expensive to replace when they fail.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The core aluminum block with cast-iron cylinder liners is incredibly robust. The lifespan of the OM642 in North America is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address profound oil leak issues in the engine valley and the extraordinarily complex emission control system failures. If the oil cooler seals are upgraded and the strict US exhaust aftertreatment system is maintained perfectly, the powertrain is magnificent.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, electronically actuated Garrett VNT turbocharger mounted directly in the center 'V' of the engine block. The electronic actuator provides incredibly precise boost control, entirely eliminating turbo lag. However, the turbocharger's intake seal is globally infamous for degrading and dripping oily PCV vapor directly onto the electronic swirl flap actuator motor located directly beneath it, causing catastrophic Limp Mode failures.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16CP31 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module mapped specifically to meet incredibly strict US EPA Tier 2 Bin 5 / SULEV emissions regulations. The ECU actively monitors an array of exhaust sensors and aggressively manages DPF regeneration cycles. The engine output is slightly restricted to 211 horsepower to manage NOx emissions. The EDC16 ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, but tuning requires careful consideration of local emissions testing.)",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 2 Bin 5 (Strict DPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM642 is vastly overbuilt and capable of handling over 600 Nm of torque natively. Because this variant is paired with the heavy-duty 722.9 automatic transmission, it is an absolute dream for tuners. A simple software flash and DPF delete completely transforms the car, safely restoring the missing European horsepower and pushing it even further.)",
