    compression: "16.5:1",
    yearRange: "2002-2004",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM612 AMG utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Unlike modern lightweight diesel engines, this timing system is massively over-engineered. It is a true 'lifetime' component that will rarely, if ever, require servicing or replacement before the engine reaches 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers, provided basic 10 000 km oil change intervals with high-quality synthetic oil are strictly respected. The chain guides are robust, though the hydraulic chain tensioner can occasionally stick at extreme mileages.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC15C6 (This early Generation 1 Common Rail system utilizes an engine-driven high-pressure pump (CP1) that pressurizes a single fuel rail. AMG modified the injection mapping and fitted specialized high-flow Bosch solenoid injectors to deliver immense volumes of fuel directly into the combustion chambers. While incredibly efficient and brutally torquey, this early CDI system is plagued by the infamous 'Black Death'—a critical failure where the copper crush washers sealing the injectors to the cylinder head fail, allowing combustion gases and tar-like diesel sludge to bury the five injectors permanently.)",
    engineLifespan: "400 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM612 cast-iron engine block is globally renowned for its legendary durability. To achieve the 3.0L displacement, AMG increased the stroke, resulting in a heavier rotating assembly. The engine will comfortably outlast the W203 chassis, but its lifespan is heavily dictated by the complex water-to-air cooling system and the specialized AMG drivetrain components. The true enemies of this vehicle's lifespan are catastrophic structural rust on the bodywork, the 'Black Death' injector seal failure destroying the cylinder head, and overheating from a failed intercooler pump.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an AMG-tuned Garrett Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) turbocharger featuring a significantly larger compressor wheel. The variable vanes adjust exhaust gas flow to spool the massive turbo quickly, providing a gargantuan 540 Nm of peak torque at a very low 2 000 RPM. This turbo is paired with a highly specialized water-to-air intercooler system, identical in principle to the C 32 AMG, which drastically lowers intake temperatures. However, the Bosch intercooler fluid pump fails constantly, causing severe power loss.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC15C6 (A highly sophisticated and reliable electronic diesel control module mapped specifically by AMG. It perfectly integrates common rail pressure monitoring, aggressive VNT turbo actuation, and the electronic EGR valve. The ECU is fully OBD-II compliant and incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to push this unique diesel engine into supercar-levels of torque.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block and specialized AMG forged internals of the OM612 5-cylinder are vastly overbuilt. The bottom end can easily handle massive boost pressures. Because this variant is paired with the heavily reinforced AMG SpeedShift 722.6 automatic transmission, it can be tuned aggressively without worrying about destroying the drivetrain. Upgrading the intercooler pump is mandatory for any tuning.)",
