      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Timing Chain Jump): If the stretched simplex timing chain skips a tooth on the worn camshaft gears, the pistons will violently smash into the open valves, entirely destroying the cylinder head.",
      "Economic Total Loss (ECU Oil Flooding): If the camshaft magnet leak is ignored, replacing the oil-soaked engine wiring harness and the Siemens ECU will easily cost upwards of 2 500 EUR.",
      "Catastrophic Supercharger Failure: Ignoring a whining or metallic grinding noise from the Eaton M45 will result in the internal rotors colliding and sending metal shrapnel directly into the engine's intake manifold.",
