    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M274 completely abandoned the catastrophic single-row design of the older M271, adopting a much more robust roller-type timing chain. While the chain itself is highly durable and rarely snaps, the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjusters are still incredibly prone to premature wear. When the internal locking pins in the VVT gears fail, the engine emits a violently loud, metallic rattling noise for 2-3 seconds during a cold start. Ignoring this rattle will eventually cause the adjusters to shatter, destroying the cylinder head. The chain tensioner is also a known weak point.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at up to 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization, lower emissions, and massive low-end torque. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the CGI system suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting every 100 000 kilometers.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum M274 block is incredibly robust, but its lifespan is entirely dictated by strict maintenance. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause catastrophic bearing wear. The water pump and electronic thermostat are also notorious for sudden failures. If the cooling system is maintained, the VVT gears replaced when they rattle, and the oil changed religiously, the engine will easily outlast the fantastic W204 chassis.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling exhaust gas turbocharger integrated directly into the exhaust manifold to minimize heat loss and maximize response. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering peak torque at an astonishingly low 1 250 RPM. However, the internal wastegate linkage is known to wear out, causing a highly annoying metallic rattle upon deceleration and a gradual loss of boost pressure. The electronic actuator can also fail due to extreme heat exposure.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of direct injection and turbocharging. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, and controls the smart alternator. It is highly robust but extremely sensitive to battery voltage drops. Tuning potential is absolutely phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the downsized 1.6-liter M274 is highly advanced and robust. Because this block was engineered for high boost applications, the stock internals are vastly overbuilt for its conservative 156hp rating. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the factory turbocharger and the strict flow limits of the high-pressure fuel pump. Pushing the engine past 260hp significantly shortens the lifespan of the connecting rods.)",
