      "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Due to direct injection, the intake valves are never washed with fuel. They build up thick carbon deposits over 80,000 km, causing rough idling, misfires, and noticeable power losses.",
      "Camshaft Magnet Oil Leak (Capillary Action): The front camshaft adjuster magnets leak oil internally into their electrical connectors. The oil wicks through the entire wiring harness, permanently destroying the Siemens ECU.",
      "Electronic Steering Lock (ESL/ELV) Failure: The tiny electric motor inside the steering column lock burns out, completely immobilizing the vehicle. The key turns but nothing happens.",
      "Turbocharger Wastegate Rattle: The internal linkage of the turbocharger wastegate wears out, causing a loud, annoying metallic rattle upon deceleration and loss of boost pressure."
