    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 utilizes a double-row timing chain. Unlike the catastrophic single-row chains of the 4-cylinder engines, this chain is incredibly robust. However, early M272 engines were globally infamous for a fatal flaw where the balance shaft chain sprocket was manufactured with insufficiently hardened steel. Fortunately, the vast majority of W204 models fall outside the affected serial number range, meaning this engine in the W204 chassis generally enjoys a highly durable, lifetime timing system. Always verify the engine serial number before purchase to be absolutely certain.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system. It utilizes modern electronic throttle control and a highly sensitive Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor. The system is extremely reliable and completely avoids the capillary oil wicking issues that plagued the 4-cylinder engines, as well as the carbon buildup issues of the later direct-injected engines. However, the variable-length intake manifold uses fragile plastic swirl flap arms that frequently break and trigger performance issues.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M272 V6 engine block in the W204 chassis is exceptional. Because it almost entirely avoided the balance shaft metallurgy issues of the older W203 generation, it is an incredibly robust, deeply refined V6. The W204 chassis completely eradicated the structural rust issues of the past. The engine will easily outlast the vehicle with basic maintenance, provided the intake manifold swirl flaps and the thermostat are addressed when they fail.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 relies entirely on its 2.5-liter displacement, high 11.2:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate its incredibly smooth power delivery. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids the complex supercharger or turbocharger maintenance issues, making the engine bay significantly simpler and highly reliable.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system designed to tightly control emissions and precisely manage the continuously variable valve timing. The ECU is incredibly robust and mounts securely on top of the engine block. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine mapped close to its natural efficiency limits, tuning potential is practically nonexistent, making the ECU a 'leave it alone' component.)",
