    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 utilizes a double-row timing chain. Unlike the catastrophic single-row chains of the 4-cylinder engines, this chain is generally incredibly robust. Because the C 300 designation largely replaced the C 280, these later-production M272 engines safely fall outside the infamous balance shaft defect serial number range that destroyed early W203s. Therefore, the timing system in this specific W204 is considered a highly durable, lifetime component, provided the engine receives regular high-quality synthetic oil changes.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system. It utilizes modern electronic throttle control and a highly sensitive Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor. The system is extremely reliable and completely avoids the capillary oil wicking issues that plagued the 4-cylinder engines, as well as the severe carbon buildup issues inherent to later direct-injected CGI engines. However, the variable-length intake manifold uses fragile plastic swirl flap arms that frequently break and trigger performance issues.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M272 V6 engine block in the W204 chassis is exceptional. By completely avoiding the balance shaft metallurgy issues of the older W203 generation, it is an incredibly robust, deeply refined V6. The W204 chassis also completely eradicated the structural rust issues of the past. The engine will easily outlast the vehicle with basic maintenance, provided the intake manifold swirl flaps and the thermostat are addressed when they fail.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 relies entirely on its 3.0-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate its incredibly smooth power delivery. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids complex supercharger or turbocharger maintenance issues, making the engine bay significantly simpler and highly reliable.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system designed to tightly control emissions and precisely manage the continuously variable valve timing. The ECU is incredibly robust and mounts securely on top of the engine block. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine mapped close to its natural efficiency limits, tuning potential is practically nonexistent, making the ECU a 'leave it alone' component.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 / Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.0-liter M272 is vastly overbuilt. However, because it is naturally aspirated, extracting any meaningful horsepower is virtually impossible without completely disassembling the engine. The block can theoretically handle forced induction, but doing so is financially and logically absurd when the massive 3.5L M272 V6 bolts right into the same engine bay.)",
