    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block on some M276 variants, but predominantly driven from the front. The M276 completely abandoned the 90-degree architecture of the M272, moving to a 60-degree V-angle. This allowed the removal of the problematic balance shaft entirely. While the primary double-row timing chain is robust, early M276 engines are infamous for secondary timing chain tensioner failures. The tensioners bleed off oil pressure when parked, causing a violent 3-second rattle on cold starts. Mercedes issued a massive technical service bulletin to install non-return check valves behind the tensioners to fix this. It MUST be checked.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.3 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors capable of firing up to 5 times per intake stroke. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization, lower emissions, and massive low-end torque. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M276 CGI system suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting every 100 000 kilometers.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The all-aluminum M276 block is a masterpiece of modern naturally aspirated engineering. By reverting to a 60-degree V6, Mercedes eliminated the balance shaft and significantly reduced internal friction. Its lifespan is entirely dictated by strict maintenance. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause bearing wear. If the timing chain tensioner check valves are installed, and the oil changed religiously, this engine is phenomenally reliable.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M276 relies entirely on its massive 3.5-liter displacement, an incredibly high 12.0:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate power. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids complex turbocharger maintenance issues. It delivers an incredibly smooth, linear torque curve that builds beautifully toward the redline.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.3 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of direct injection and multi-spark ignition. This specific ECU mapping is the absolute holy grail for tuners: it artificially software-restricts the massive 3.5L engine to just 252 horsepower (down from the C 350's 306 horsepower) purely for marketing and tax bracket purposes. A software flash entirely removes this digital handicap.)",
