    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 CGI utilizes the same robust double-row timing chain as the standard M272. Because it was introduced later in the production cycle (2008+), this engine entirely avoids the catastrophic balance shaft metallurgy issues of the earlier W203 generation. Therefore, the timing system in this specific W204 is considered a highly durable, lifetime component, provided the engine receives regular high-quality synthetic oil changes. However, the high-pressure fuel pump introduces new mechanical loads on the valvetrain.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7 (This is an early and highly complex Gasoline Direct Injection (CGI) system utilizing 'Stratified Charge' lean-burn technology. It features a mechanically driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) that injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber via ultra-fast Piezoelectric injectors at up to 200 bar. While this provides massive fuel efficiency and a 20hp bump over the manifold-injected version, it introduces devastating vulnerabilities. The HPFP frequently leaks internally, diluting the engine oil with raw gasoline. Furthermore, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the CGI system suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting to clean.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M272 CGI block is heavily compromised by the direct injection system. The core block is practically immortal, but if the HPFP leaks internally and the gasoline-thinned oil is not caught immediately, the engine bearings will seize. The complex stratified charge system also relies on fragile NOx sensors and cats. The W204 chassis completely eradicated structural rust, but the engine requires extreme, hyper-vigilant maintenance to survive high mileages.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 CGI relies entirely on its massive 3.5-liter displacement, an incredibly high 12.2:1 compression ratio, and direct injection to generate power. Because it lacks forced induction, it avoids turbocharger lag, delivering a highly responsive, aggressive, and perfectly linear torque curve that builds relentlessly toward the redline.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of stratified charge direct injection. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the lean-burn cycles, and relies heavily on expensive NOx sensors in the exhaust. The ECU is highly robust but will throw constant codes if the direct injection system or NOx sensors degrade slightly.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 / Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.5-liter M272 CGI is vastly overbuilt. However, the incredibly high 12.2:1 compression ratio makes this engine highly susceptible to detonation if tuned improperly. Extracting any meaningful horsepower is virtually impossible without forced induction, which is completely unviable given the high compression and complex piezo direct injection limits.)",
