      blockDesign: "The M272.971 is a 90-degree V6 featuring a highly rigid all-aluminum closed-deck block with Silitec cylinder liners. This specific coating reduces internal friction and wear without the need for heavy iron sleeves. Because a 90-degree V-angle creates inherent secondary harmonic vibrations, Mercedes engineered a counter-rotating balance shaft located deep in the engine valley, driven directly by the timing chain, resulting in incredible, V8-like smoothness.",
      crankshaft: "Forged Steel, supported by 4 main bearings. The stroke is increased to 86mm compared to the smaller 3.0L C 300 variant, providing the massive torque increase.",
