      "PCV Valve Failure: The crankcase ventilation valve fails, causing the engine to consume massive amounts of oil and emit a high-pitched squeal or whistle at idle.",
      "Intake Manifold Leaks: The magnesium intake manifold develops cracks or gasket leaks, causing rough idling and lean codes.",
      "Electronic Steering Lock (ESL/ELV) Failure: The tiny electric motor inside the steering column lock burns out, completely immobilizing the vehicle. The key turns, but the car will not crank.",
