    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M156 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Because the Black Series was built late in the M156's lifecycle, it is equipped with the revised M157-style head bolts from the factory, entirely eliminating the catastrophic head bolt snapping issue of early M156s. However, the true fatal flaw of the valvetrain remains: the camshafts and the hydraulic lifters. The Black Series features the hardened SLS AMG lifters natively, but the camshaft lobes remain susceptible to severe wear if oil intervals are neglected or the car is aggressively driven while cold.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system mapped specifically by AMG for the Black Series. Unlike modern AMG engines, the M156 uses traditional port injection rather than direct injection. This was a deliberate choice to allow the massive 6.2-liter engine to breathe freely and rev aggressively to its 7,200 RPM redline without the flow limitations of early direct injection systems. Because it uses port injection, the M156 completely avoids the severe carbon buildup issues that plague modern engines. The fuel delivery is violently responsive, matched perfectly to the aggressive track-focused ECU mapping.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 350 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the Black Series engine is excellent compared to early M156 variants. Because the catastrophic head bolt issue was resolved, and it features the forged internal rotating assembly from the SLS AMG supercar (shedding 3 kg of rotating mass), the bottom end is virtually indestructible. If the oil is changed religiously every 5 000 km to protect the camshafts, the core engine block will last a very long time. However, Black Series models are frequently subjected to intense track use, which exponentially increases wear on the transmission and cooling systems.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The Black Series relies entirely on its gargantuan 6.2-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and aggressive camshaft profiles to generate 517 horsepower natively. Because it lacks forced induction, it delivers an utterly visceral, instantaneous throttle response that modern turbocharged AMG engines simply cannot replicate. The SLS AMG lightweight forged rotating assembly allows the engine to rev with terrifying speed, screaming toward the redline.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system completely bespoke to AMG. In the Black Series, the ECU mapping is specifically revised by AMG to fully utilize the SLS internal hardware and the vastly upgraded cooling system, raising the output to 517 horsepower. This pushes the naturally aspirated M156 very close to its maximum reliable limits without physical modifications, though tuners can still optimize spark timing for minor gains.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "650+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the Black Series is genuinely race-grade. Featuring authentic SLS AMG forged pistons, lightweight connecting rods, and a strengthened crankshaft, the bottom end is immensely strong. With long-tube headers and a tune, the engine comfortably pushes 570+ hp naturally aspirated. Bolting on an aftermarket supercharger kit can easily push this forged block past 700+ hp, limited only by the MCT transmission clutches and rear tire traction.)",
