      "PCV Valve Failure: The crankcase ventilation valve located at the rear of the intake manifold fails frequently. The internal diaphragm tears, causing the engine to consume massive amounts of oil and emitting a distinct high-pitched squeal or whistle at idle.",
      "Intake Manifold Gasket Leaks & Cracking: The dual-plenum magnesium intake manifold develops vacuum leaks at the central gasket or cracks internally due to extreme heat cycling. This causes rough idling and lean running conditions.",
      "Electronic Steering Lock (ESL/ELV) Failure: THE defining chassis flaw of the W204. The tiny electric motor inside the steering column lock burns out, completely immobilizing the vehicle. The key turns, but the car will not crank.",
