      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Black Death): Ignoring a leaking injector seal will result in the injector fusing permanently to the aluminum cylinder head, requiring the entire head to be removed and machined at immense cost.",
      "Transmission Control Module Destruction: Capillary action from a leaking 13-pin connector on the 722.6 gearbox will push ATF into the passenger footwell, soaking and permanently destroying the expensive TCM.",
      "DPF / Exhaust Choking: A clogged EGR valve or a stuck-open thermostat will prevent the engine from initiating a DPF regeneration cycle, causing the exhaust to plug up entirely and stranding the vehicle in Limp Mode."
