      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Swirl Flaps): If the plastic intake swirl flaps snap off and enter the combustion chamber, they will destroy the valves, pistons, and turbocharger instantly.",
      "Immobilization (ESL/ELV Failure): A burnt-out steering lock motor will leave you completely stranded without warning. Repairing this at the dealership is highly expensive; aftermarket emulators offer a cheaper fix.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Black Death): Ignoring a leaking injector seal will result in the injector fusing permanently to the aluminum cylinder head, requiring the entire head to be removed and machined at immense cost.",
