    generation: "W204 (2007-2014) - Facelift",
    engineCode: "OM 651.913",
    profileId: "om651913-c200cdi",
    displacement: "2,143 cc",
    power: "136 hp (100 kW)",
    torque: "360 Nm",
    fuelType: "Diesel",
    cylinders: 4,
    valves: 16,
    compression: "16.2:1",
    yearRange: "2010-2014",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 represents a massive architectural shift, moving the timing chain to the gearbox side to reduce engine height for pedestrian safety regulations. This simplex chain is highly prone to stretching over high mileages. When it stretches, it causes a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Crucially, because it is located at the back of the engine, replacing the timing chain is an incredibly labor-intensive and expensive job, often requiring the engine or transmission to be completely removed from the vehicle.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi CRD 3.xx (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at up to 2 000 bar. This specific mid-output variant utilizes highly reliable Bosch electromagnetic solenoid injectors, deliberately avoiding the catastrophic Delphi Piezo injector failures that plagued the higher-output OM651 models. This makes the fuel system on the C 200 CDI remarkably dependable, though it still requires high-quality fuel to prevent high-pressure pump wear.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM651 cast-iron engine block is exceptionally robust. Because this specific C 200 CDI variant is heavily software-restricted to just 136 horsepower, the internal rotating assembly experiences virtually no mechanical stress. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W204 chassis. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures (DPF/EGR), the notorious coolant leaks from the plastic water neck, and the eventual, highly expensive rear timing chain replacement.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) turbocharger. Unlike the highly complex bi-turbo setups on higher output models, this single turbo provides a simpler, highly reliable boost curve. The variable vanes dynamically adjust exhaust gas velocity to spool the compressor instantly, providing the full 360 Nm of peak torque at a very low 1 600 RPM. Because the engine is restricted to 136 horsepower, the turbo operates well below its thermal limits. However, the vanes can jam with carbon if driven exclusively in the city.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD 3.xx (A lightning-fast, highly complex electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 2000 bar common rail pressure monitoring, precise VNT turbo actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the DPF regeneration cycles. This specific ECU is hard-coded with a severe mapping restriction to limit the engine to exactly 136hp. The ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to completely erase the factory handicap.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. The limiting factor for horsepower is the single VNT turbocharger and the flow capacity of the factory solenoid injectors. Because this block is physically identical to the higher-output versions, it can easily handle massive boost. Upgrading to the bi-turbo setup and Piezo injectors from the C 250 CDI is possible but financially illogical.)",
