    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 represents a massive architectural shift, moving the timing chain to the gearbox side to reduce engine height for pedestrian safety regulations. This simplex chain is highly prone to stretching over high mileages. When it stretches, it causes a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Crucially, because it is located at the back of the engine, replacing the timing chain is an incredibly labor-intensive and expensive job, often requiring the engine or transmission to be completely removed from the vehicle.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi CRD 3.xx (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at up to 2 000 bar. This specific eco-optimized 'Edition' variant typically features the highly reliable Bosch electromagnetic solenoid injectors, deliberately avoiding the catastrophic Piezo injector failures that plagued earlier OM651 models. This makes the fuel system remarkably dependable, though it still requires high-quality fuel to prevent high-pressure pump wear.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM651 cast-iron engine block is exceptionally robust. Because this specific 'Edition' variant is software-restricted in both horsepower (163hp) and torque (capped at 360 Nm for maximum fuel efficiency and aerodynamic tire protection), the internal rotating assembly experiences virtually no mechanical stress. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures (DPF/EGR), the notorious coolant leaks from the plastic water neck, and the eventual, highly expensive rear timing chain replacement.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly complex 2-stage sequential turbocharger system. It utilizes a small, high-pressure BorgWarner turbocharger that spools instantly off idle to eliminate turbo lag, seamlessly handing over boost duties to a larger, low-pressure turbocharger as RPMs increase. While brilliant for performance and efficiency, the complex vacuum actuation system and immense heat generation make it significantly more difficult and expensive to service than a single turbo. In this Edition model, boost is heavily governed for eco-mapping.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD 3.xx (A lightning-fast, highly complex electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 2000 bar common rail pressure monitoring, the incredibly complex sequential twin-turbo vacuum actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the DPF regeneration cycles. This specific ECU is hard-coded with a severe mapping restriction to limit both horsepower and torque for the BlueEFFICIENCY eco targets. The ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to completely erase the eco-handicap.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "250+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. Because the C 220 CDI utilizes the identical 2-stage twin-turbo setup as the 204-horsepower C 250 CDI, the hardware is capable of massive power gains. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the engine to C 250 CDI power levels and beyond, completely ignoring the factory eco-restrictions.)",
