    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi CRD 3.xx (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at up to 2 000 bar. This fleet variant utilizes highly reliable Bosch electromagnetic solenoid injectors, deliberately avoiding the catastrophic Piezo injector failures that plagued the early OM651 models. This makes the fuel system on the C 220 CDI remarkably dependable, though it still requires high-quality fuel to prevent high-pressure pump wear.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM651 cast-iron engine block is exceptionally robust. Because this specific C 220 CDI variant is software-restricted to 163 horsepower (to slip under 120 kW tax brackets) but maintains the full 400 Nm of torque, the internal rotating assembly experiences virtually no mechanical stress. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W204 chassis. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures (DPF/EGR), the notorious coolant leaks from the plastic water neck, and the eventual, highly expensive rear timing chain replacement.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly complex 2-stage sequential turbocharger system. It utilizes a small, high-pressure BorgWarner turbocharger that spools instantly off idle to eliminate turbo lag, seamlessly handing over boost duties to a much larger, low-pressure turbocharger as RPMs increase. This provides an incredibly flat, muscular torque curve of 400 Nm from just 1 400 RPM. While brilliant for performance, the complex vacuum actuation system and immense heat generation make it significantly more difficult and expensive to service than a single turbo.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD 3.xx (A lightning-fast, highly complex electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 2000 bar common rail pressure monitoring, precise sequential turbo actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the DPF regeneration cycles. This specific ECU is hard-coded with a mapping restriction to limit the engine to exactly 120kW (163hp) for fleet/tax purposes. The ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to completely erase the tax handicap.)",
