    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 represents a massive architectural shift, moving the timing chain to the gearbox side to reduce engine height for pedestrian safety regulations. This simplex chain is highly prone to stretching over high mileages, exacerbated by the massive 500 Nm of torque in the C 250. When it stretches, it causes a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Crucially, because it is located at the back of the engine, replacing the timing chain is an incredibly labor-intensive and expensive job, often requiring the engine or transmission to be completely removed from the vehicle.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi CRD 3.xx (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at up to 2 000 bar. This specific C 250 CDI variant is globally infamous for its initial use of Delphi Piezoelectric fuel injectors. These Piezo injectors failed catastrophically and repeatedly across the entire Mercedes lineup, causing massive class-action lawsuits. Mercedes was forced to issue a global recall to replace the incredibly fragile Piezo injectors with highly reliable electromagnetic solenoid injectors, along with a revised ECU map and engine wiring harness. If purchasing this vehicle, you MUST physically verify that the injectors have been swapped to solenoids.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM651 cast-iron engine block is exceptionally robust. Assuming the factory Piezo injector recall was performed and the car is now running solenoid injectors, the engine block itself is virtually indestructible. However, the immense 500 Nm of torque puts severe strain on the drivetrain, frequently destroying the dual-mass flywheel on manual models. The lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures (DPF/EGR), the notorious coolant leaks from the plastic water neck, and the eventual, highly expensive rear timing chain replacement.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly complex 2-stage sequential turbocharger system. It utilizes a small, high-pressure BorgWarner KP39 turbocharger that spools instantly off idle to eliminate turbo lag, seamlessly handing over boost duties to a much larger, low-pressure K04 turbocharger as RPMs increase. This provides an incredible, V8-rivaling torque curve of 500 Nm from just 1 600 RPM all the way to the redline. While brilliant for performance, the complex vacuum actuation system and immense heat generation make it significantly more difficult and expensive to service than a single turbo.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD 3.xx (A lightning-fast, highly complex electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 2000 bar common rail pressure monitoring, the incredibly complex sequential twin-turbo vacuum actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the DPF regeneration cycles. If the factory injector recall was performed, the ECU was re-flashed by the dealership to operate the new solenoid injectors. The ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to extract massive horsepower from the twin-turbo setup.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
