    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi CRD 3.xx (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at up to 2 000 bar. This specific C 250 CDI variant is globally infamous for its initial use of Delphi Piezoelectric fuel injectors. These Piezo injectors failed catastrophically and repeatedly across the entire Mercedes lineup, causing massive class-action lawsuits. Mercedes was forced to issue a global recall to replace the incredibly fragile Piezo injectors with highly reliable electromagnetic solenoid injectors, along with a revised ECU map and engine wiring harness. If purchasing this vehicle, you MUST physically verify that the injectors have been swapped to solenoids.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM651 cast-iron engine block is exceptionally robust. Because this specific C 250 CDI variant is heavily software-restricted to just 163 horsepower for specific corporate fleet tax brackets, the internal rotating assembly experiences absolutely zero mechanical stress. Assuming the factory Piezo injector recall was performed and the car is now running solenoid injectors, the engine block itself is virtually indestructible. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures (DPF/EGR), the notorious coolant leaks from the plastic water neck, and the eventual, highly expensive rear timing chain replacement.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly complex 2-stage sequential turbocharger system. It utilizes a small, high-pressure BorgWarner KP39 turbocharger that spools instantly off idle to eliminate turbo lag, seamlessly handing over boost duties to a much larger, low-pressure K04 turbocharger as RPMs increase. This provides an incredible torque curve of 400 Nm from just 1 400 RPM. Because the engine is artificially restricted to 163 horsepower, the twin-turbos operate well below their thermal limits. However, the complex vacuum actuation system makes it significantly more difficult and expensive to service.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD 3.xx (A lightning-fast, highly complex electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 2000 bar common rail pressure monitoring, the incredibly complex sequential twin-turbo vacuum actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the DPF regeneration cycles. This specific ECU is hard-coded with a severe mapping restriction to limit the engine to exactly 163hp (120kW) for tax purposes. The ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to completely erase the tax handicap and restore full C 250 power.)",
