      blockDesign: "The OM651 features an incredibly robust cast-iron block with an aluminum cylinder head. It represents a massive paradigm shift in Mercedes engine architecture. The timing chain was moved to the rear of the engine (gearbox side) to lower the engine height at the front, aiding in pedestrian impact safety regulations. This design choice makes timing chain replacement exceptionally difficult.",
