    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block on this W204 setup. The OM642 utilizes a simplex (single-row) timing chain. While significantly more durable than the catastrophic gasoline M271 chains, it is known to stretch over high mileages (250 000+ km) due to the immense torque of the V6. When it stretches, it causes timing correlation errors and a distinct cold-start rattle. Replacing it is highly labor-intensive due to the V6 packaging in the compact W204 engine bay.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17CP46 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at 1 600 bar via a Bosch CP3 pump. It utilizes lightning-fast piezo injectors capable of multiple precisely timed injections per stroke. This entirely eradicates traditional diesel clatter, making the V6 sound incredibly smooth and refined. However, these piezo injectors are extremely sensitive to poor fuel quality and are astronomically expensive to replace when they fail.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The core aluminum block with cast-iron cylinder liners is incredibly robust. The lifespan of the OM642 is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address profound oil leak issues in the engine valley and complex emission control system failures. This engine is paired with the highly robust 7G-Tronic transmission and 4MATIC system, completely avoiding the catastrophic manual transmission failures. If the oil cooler seals are upgraded and the intake tract kept clean, the powertrain is magnificent.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, electronically actuated Garrett VNT turbocharger mounted directly in the center 'V' of the engine block. The electronic actuator provides incredibly precise boost control, entirely eliminating turbo lag and delivering 540 Nm natively. However, the turbocharger's intake seal is globally infamous for degrading and dripping oily PCV vapor directly onto the electronic swirl flap actuator motor located directly beneath it, causing catastrophic Limp Mode failures.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17CP46 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the piezo injectors, VNT turbo, EGR, and factory DPF systems. This ECU mapping unleashes the engine's 540 Nm of torque perfectly matched with the robust 7-speed automatic gearbox and 4MATIC all-wheel drive. The EDC17 ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to easily unlock massive performance gains.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM642 is vastly overbuilt and capable of handling over 650 Nm of torque natively. Because this variant is paired with the heavy-duty 722.9 automatic transmission and 4MATIC, it is an absolute dream for tuners. A simple software flash and DPF delete completely transforms the car into an incredibly fast, torque-rich muscle diesel with incredible off-the-line traction.)",
