    yearRange: "2012-2014",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM642 utilizes a simplex (single-row) timing chain. Due to the staggering 620 Nm of torque produced by this high-output variant, the chain is subjected to immense stress. While the chain itself rarely snaps, it is highly prone to stretching over high mileages (200 000+ km). When it stretches, it causes timing correlation errors and a distinct cold-start rattle. Replacing it is highly labor-intensive due to the V6 packaging.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17CP46 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure Generation 4 Common Rail system operating at an incredible 2 000 bar via a revised Bosch pump. It utilizes lightning-fast piezo injectors capable of multiple precisely timed injections per stroke. This entirely eradicates traditional diesel clatter, making the V6 sound incredibly smooth and refined. However, these piezo injectors are extremely sensitive to poor fuel quality and are astronomically expensive to replace when they fail.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (This represents the 'LS' (LeistungsSteigerung) generation of the OM642 block, featuring heavily revised internals, lower compression, and enhanced cooling to handle the massive 620 Nm of torque. The core aluminum block with cast-iron cylinder liners remains incredibly robust. The lifespan is dictated by the owner's willingness to address the notorious oil cooler seal leaks, complex emission control system failures, and meticulous transmission fluid changes to protect the 7G-Tronic Plus from the immense torque.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, electronically actuated, water-cooled ball-bearing Garrett VNT turbocharger mounted directly in the center 'V' of the engine block. This specific LS-variant turbo provides incredibly precise boost control and incredibly fast spool times, delivering the full 620 Nm of torque natively. However, the turbocharger's intake seal is globally infamous for degrading and dripping oily PCV vapor directly onto the electronic swirl flap actuator motor located directly beneath it, causing Limp Mode failures.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17CP46 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the piezo injectors, water-cooled VNT turbo, EGR, and factory DPF systems. This ECU mapping unleashes the engine's staggering 620 Nm of torque, perfectly matched with the robust 7-speed automatic gearbox. The EDC17 ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to easily unlock supercar levels of torque.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 / Euro 6 (Factory DPF & AdBlue/BlueTEC Equipped on some models)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM642 'LS' is vastly overbuilt, featuring specific cooling channels to handle high EGTs. Because this variant is paired with the heavy-duty 722.9 automatic transmission, it is an absolute dream for tuners. A simple software flash completely transforms the car into an incredibly fast, torque-rich muscle diesel, easily surpassing 700 Nm of torque without stressing the bottom end.)",
