    cylinders: 4,
    valves: 16,
    compression: "10.3:1",
    yearRange: "2014-2018",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M274 utilizes a roller-type timing chain. While significantly more reliable than the catastrophic simplex chains of the older M271 generation, the M274 is globally infamous for Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjuster failures. The internal locking pins inside the VVT phasers shear off, causing a violently loud, 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the loose phaser can cause the timing chain to skip or snap. Preventative replacement of the VVT gears and the chain tensioner is required if the cold-start rattle develops.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at up to 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization and efficiency. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M274 suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting every 100 000 kilometers. The HPFP is also prone to leaking internally, diluting the engine oil with raw gasoline.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum M274 block is incredibly robust, but its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by strict maintenance. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause catastrophic bearing wear. The water pump, featuring a complex vacuum-actuated shroud, and the electronic thermostat are notorious for sudden failures. If the cooling system is maintained, the VVT gears replaced when they rattle, and the oil changed religiously, the core engine will last a very long time.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling exhaust gas IHI turbocharger integrated closely with the exhaust manifold to minimize heat loss and maximize response. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering 250 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. However, the internal wastegate linkage and the electronic actuator are known to wear out over high mileages, causing a metallic rattle upon deceleration and a gradual loss of boost pressure.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of direct injection and turbocharging. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, and controls the smart alternator. Tuning potential is absolutely phenomenal via the OBD-II port, safely unlocking over 180 horsepower from the 1.6L block.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the downsized 1.6-liter M274 is highly advanced and robust. Because this specific block was engineered to withstand high torque, the stock internals are vastly overbuilt for its 156hp rating. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the factory IHI turbocharger and the flow limits of the high-pressure fuel pump. Pushing the 1.6L block past 250hp significantly shortens the lifespan of the connecting rods.)",
    fuelConsumption: {
      city: "7.2 - 8.8 L/100km",
      highway: "5.0 - 6.2 L/100km",
      mixed: "5.8 - 7.0 L/100km",
      sporty: "9.5+ L/100km"
    },
    oilSpecification: "6.0L 5W-40 Synthetic (MB 229.5 strictly required. Checking the oil dipstick weekly for the smell of gasoline is absolutely mandatory on direct injection models.)",
    commonIssues: [
      "VVT Camshaft Adjuster Rattle: The internal locking mechanism in the camshaft gears fails, causing a loud 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. Must be fixed to prevent engine destruction.",
      "Water Pump Failure: The M274 water pump features a vacuum-controlled plastic shroud designed to block coolant flow for faster warm-up. This shroud jams, or the pump bearings fail, causing rapid overheating and coolant leaks.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Leaks: The mechanical fuel pump can leak internally, sending raw gasoline directly into the engine oil and destroying its lubricity.",
      "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Due to direct injection, the intake valves build up thick carbon deposits, causing rough idling, misfires, and noticeable power losses.",
      "Thermostat Failure: The electronically controlled thermostat frequently fails open or closed, triggering Check Engine lights and causing cooling anomalies.",
      "W205 Interior Creaks & Touchpad Failure: The W205 introduced a stunning new interior, but early models suffer from severe creaking in the center console (especially Piano Black trim), and the center COMAND touchpad/rotary dial frequently fails."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Fuel Dilution): If the HPFP internal leak is ignored, the gasoline-thinned oil will fail to protect the main and rod bearings, causing the engine to completely seize.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (VVT Failure): If the cold start rattle is ignored for tens of thousands of kilometers, the camshaft adjusters can disintegrate and destroy the timing chain system.",
      "Overheating (Water Pump/Thermostat): Sudden failure of the complex water pump or the electronic thermostat will cause the aluminum block to overheat rapidly and potentially warp the cylinder head.",
      "Economic Total Loss (Turbocharger Actuator): The electronic wastegate actuator on the turbocharger can fail due to extreme heat. Mercedes often mandates replacing the entire turbocharger assembly rather than just the actuator, costing thousands.",
      "PCV System Failure: The crankcase ventilation system fails, pushing raw oil into the intake tract and turbocharger, severely exacerbating the carbon buildup issue and causing smoke."
    ],
