    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M274 utilizes a roller-type timing chain. While significantly more reliable than the catastrophic simplex chains of the older M271 generation, the M274 is globally infamous for Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjuster failures. The internal locking pins inside the VVT phasers shear off, causing a violently loud, 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the loose phaser can cause the timing chain to skip or snap. Preventative replacement of the VVT gears and the chain tensioner is required if the cold-start rattle develops.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at up to 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization and efficiency. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M274 suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting every 100 000 kilometers. The HPFP is also prone to leaking internally, diluting the engine oil with raw gasoline.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L M274 block is incredibly robust, but its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by strict maintenance. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause catastrophic bearing wear. The water pump, featuring a complex vacuum-actuated shroud, and the electronic thermostat are notorious for sudden failures. If the cooling system is maintained, the VVT gears replaced when they rattle, and the oil changed religiously, the core engine will last a very long time.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling exhaust gas IHI turbocharger integrated closely with the exhaust manifold to minimize heat loss and maximize response. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering 300 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. However, the internal wastegate linkage and the electronic actuator are known to wear out over high mileages, causing a metallic rattle upon deceleration and a gradual loss of boost pressure.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of direct injection and turbocharging. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, and controls the smart alternator. Because this 2.0L block is identical to the 211hp C 250 and 245hp C 300, the 184hp C 200 is artificially restricted by software, making its tuning potential absolutely phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M274 is highly advanced and robust. Because this specific block was engineered to withstand high torque in the heavier GLC and E-Class models, the stock internals are vastly overbuilt for its conservative 184hp rating in the C 200. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the factory IHI turbocharger. Pushing the 2.0L block past 280hp safely requires an upgraded downpipe to manage EGTs.)",
