    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M264 engine heavily revised the timing architecture from the older M274. It utilizes a robust roller-type timing chain. Mercedes significantly improved the durability of the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) adjusters, making the catastrophic cold-start rattles of the previous generation much less common. However, it is still a complex chain system that requires pristine, frequent oil changes to maintain proper tensioner pressure.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.x (A state-of-the-art, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at pressures exceeding 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M264 still suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract over time, requiring physical walnut blasting. Furthermore, European facelift models are equipped with a Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF/OPF) to meet Euro 6d-TEMP emissions.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (Due to complaints about the anemic 1.5L engine, Mercedes quietly swapped the C 200 back to this detuned 2.0L block late in the facelift cycle. The all-aluminum 2.0L M264 block is a highly refined and robust unit featuring CONICSHAPE internal cylinder honing. Because it is artificially restricted to 197hp (sharing hardware with the 258hp C 300), the core engine block experiences virtually zero mechanical stress and is virtually indestructible. However, the lifespan is heavily dictated by the incredibly fragile 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid system, which is astronomically expensive to repair.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling twin-scroll exhaust gas turbocharger integrated closely with the exhaust manifold. This twin-scroll setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering peak 320 Nm torque remarkably early. Because this specific 2.0L C 200 variant is software-restricted to just 197 horsepower, the turbocharger operates incredibly far below its thermal and mechanical limits.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the combustion engine with the 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid system. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery, manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure. Tuning potential is absolutely phenomenal because this is physically a detuned C 300 engine.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with GPF/OPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M264 is vastly overbuilt. Because this specific block shares its core architecture with the higher-output C 300 (which pushes 258hp natively), the stock internals are laughing at the conservative 197hp rating. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the factory turbocharger, the strict thermal limits of the GPF exhaust filter, and the ECU torque limits protecting the 48V BSG system.)",
