    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M264 engine heavily revised the timing architecture from the older M274. It utilizes a robust roller-type timing chain. Mercedes significantly improved the durability of the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) adjusters, making the catastrophic cold-start rattles of the previous generation much less common. However, it is still a complex chain system that requires pristine, frequent oil changes to maintain proper tensioner pressure.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.x (A state-of-the-art, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at pressures exceeding 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M264 still suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract over time, requiring physical walnut blasting. Furthermore, European facelift models are equipped with a Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF/OPF) to meet Euro 6d-TEMP emissions.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L M264 block is a highly refined and robust unit featuring CONICSHAPE internal cylinder honing. Mechanically, the core engine block is exceptionally strong. However, the lifespan and economic viability of this specific C 300 variant are heavily dictated by the 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid system. The belt-driven starter-generator (BSG), the 48V lithium-ion battery, and the 48V-to-12V DC/DC converter are notoriously fragile and astronomically expensive to replace when they fail out of warranty. If the 48V system fails, the car becomes completely immobilized.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling twin-scroll exhaust gas turbocharger integrated closely with the exhaust manifold. This twin-scroll setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, working in tandem with the 48V electric motor to provide seamless, instantaneous torque off the line before the turbo fully spools.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the combustion engine with the 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid system. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery, manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure. Tuning potential is phenomenal, pushing the 2.0L block to incredibly high outputs.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with GPF/OPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "320+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M264 is vastly overbuilt. The stock internals are capable of handling significantly more boost. The true limitation for massive power is the flow capacity of the factory twin-scroll turbocharger, the strict thermal limits of the GPF exhaust filter, and the ECU torque limits protecting the 48V BSG system.)",
