      "Overheating (Water Pump/Thermostat): Sudden failure of the complex vacuum-actuated water pump shroud or the electronic thermostat will restrict coolant flow. If the driver ignores the temperature warnings, the aluminum block will overheat rapidly, potentially warping the cylinder head and blowing the head gasket.",
      "Exhaust Choking (GPF/OPF Clogging): European facelift models feature a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter. If driven exclusively in stop-and-go city traffic without reaching high exhaust temperatures, or if incorrect non-Low-SAPS oil is used, the filter will permanently clog, forcing Limp Mode and requiring an immensely expensive replacement.",
      "Economic Total Loss (Turbocharger Assembly): The electronic wastegate actuator on the twin-scroll turbocharger is highly vulnerable to extreme heat cycling. When the actuator fails, Mercedes-Benz often mandates replacing the entire turbocharger assembly rather than just the actuator, leading to repair bills easily exceeding 2 000 EUR.",
      "Severe Power Loss (Intake Carbon Buildup): Due to the direct injection architecture, fuel no longer washes the back of the intake valves. Over tens of thousands of kilometers, thick, rock-hard carbon deposits choke the intake tract, leading to violent cold-start misfires, rough idling, and a severe loss of throttle response until physically walnut blasted.",
