    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M274 utilizes a roller-type timing chain. While significantly more reliable than the catastrophic simplex chains of the older M271 generation, the M274 is globally infamous for Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjuster failures. The internal locking pins inside the VVT phasers shear off, causing a violently loud, 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the loose phaser can cause the timing chain to skip or snap. Preventative replacement of the VVT gears and the chain tensioner is required if the cold-start rattle develops.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber at up to 200 bar. This results in incredible fuel atomization and efficiency. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M274 suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting every 60 000 miles. The HPFP is also prone to leaking internally, diluting the engine oil with raw gasoline.)",
    engineLifespan: "UNKNOWN / HIGH RISK (This specific 2014-2015 early production run of the M274 block is globally infamous for a catastrophic metallurgical defect regarding the piston wrist pins. An incredibly severe knocking noise from the engine block usually indicates impending catastrophic failure. Mercedes-Benz issued a massive technical service bulletin to rebuild these engines, requiring complete disassembly. If you are looking at a 2014-2015 model, you MUST verify that the engine was either replaced or rebuilt by the dealership; otherwise, the engine is a ticking time bomb.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling exhaust gas IHI turbocharger integrated closely with the exhaust manifold to minimize heat loss and maximize response. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering 273 lb-ft of torque incredibly early in the rev range. Because the US-market C 300 operates near the highest factory boost limit for this block, the internal wastegate linkage and the electronic actuator are highly prone to wearing out over high mileages, causing a metallic rattle upon deceleration and a gradual loss of boost pressure.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.2 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the extremely narrow operating windows of direct injection and turbocharging. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, and controls the smart alternator. Because this ECU natively runs the 2.0L block at its maximum factory mapping specifically for US EPA emissions, it provides blistering performance out of the box, with excellent tuning potential via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "N/A (DO NOT TUNE UNTIL VERIFIED. Because of the catastrophic wrist pin defect on these specific early models, applying a Stage 1 tune will immediately destroy the engine by putting excess stress on the defective components. If the engine block has been verified as rebuilt by Mercedes, it can safely handle 300+ hp.)",
