    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M274 utilizes a roller-type timing chain. While significantly more reliable than older generations, the M274 is globally infamous for Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjuster failures. The internal locking pins shear off, causing a violently loud, 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. In a PHEV application where the engine constantly turns on and off while driving, this wear is severely accelerated. Preventative replacement of the VVT gears and chain tensioner is strictly required if the rattle develops.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.x (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M274 suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract. The HPFP is also prone to leaking internally, diluting the engine oil with raw gasoline. Furthermore, European facelift models are equipped with a Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF/OPF).)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L M274 engine block is robust, but the lifespan of the C 300 e is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of the Plug-in Hybrid system. The engine operates under severe, unique stresses: the internal combustion engine is frequently turned on and off violently while driving, meaning it is often subjected to full load while completely cold. This massive thermal shock accelerates wear on the head gasket, turbocharger, and VVT gears. Furthermore, the high-voltage battery degrades over time, and its replacement cost often exceeds the value of the car.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling exhaust gas IHI turbocharger. The physical turbo is identical to the C 250/C 300, but in this PHEV application, the massive instant torque from the electric motor completely masks any turbo lag. The internal wastegate linkage and the electronic actuator are highly prone to wearing out over high mileages, causing a metallic rattle upon deceleration.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.x (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system that must seamlessly integrate the 211hp combustion engine with the 122hp electric motor sandwiched inside the transmission. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery state, regenerative braking, manages the transitions between pure EV mode and hybrid mode, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with GPF/OPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "320+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M274 is highly advanced and robust. The engine natively produces 211hp. However, pushing the combustion engine further via tuning is incredibly risky on the C 300 e, as the 9-speed transmission is already dealing with a massive 700 Nm of combined system torque. Pushing past this limit will rapidly destroy the transmission clutch packs.)",
