    yearRange: "2016-2018",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The M276 BiTurbo utilizes an incredibly complex multi-chain system. While fundamentally robust, early production models suffer from secondary chain tensioner failures. The lack of oil pressure at startup causes the chain to slap against the guides, creating a loud 3-5 second metallic rattle. Mercedes issued a technical service bulletin to install non-return check valves in the tensioners to hold oil pressure. If you hear the rattle, the repair is extremely expensive due to the incredibly tight V6 packaging.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.3 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven twin High-Pressure Fuel Pumps (HPFP) inject fuel directly into the combustion chamber. However, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M276 suffers from severe, performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting. The high-pressure pumps are also known to wear and leak internally over high mileages.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum 3.0L BiTurbo M276 block is a masterpiece of engineering. It features NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating which practically eliminates piston friction and wear. However, its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by strict maintenance. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause catastrophic bearing wear. If the timing chain tensioners are updated and the oil changed religiously, the core engine is bulletproof.)",
    turboType: "Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with two advanced, fast-spooling IHI turbochargers, one mounted directly to each cylinder bank. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering a massive 520 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. In the C 43 AMG, these turbos are run at higher boost pressures compared to the standard C 400. They are generally highly reliable, though vacuum lines controlling the wastegates can crack from intense engine bay heat.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.3 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the dual turbos and piezoelectric direct injection. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, and controls the AMG Performance 4MATIC system's torque delivery. Tuning potential is absolutely phenomenal via the OBD-II port, unlocking true supercar performance.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.0-liter BiTurbo M276 is incredibly advanced and vastly overbuilt. The stock internals handle the 367hp rating effortlessly. The engine can easily be tuned to over 420 horsepower with just a software flash. Pushing past 450hp safely requires upgraded downpipes and cooling modifications, but the block itself can withstand immense pressure.)",
