    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The M276 BiTurbo utilizes an incredibly complex multi-chain system. While early models suffered from tensioner issues, this facelifted 390hp variant comes from the factory with the updated tensioners and check valves already installed, making the timing system incredibly robust. However, due to the immense stress of the 390hp output, it still requires pristine, frequent oil changes to maintain proper hydraulic tensioner pressure over high mileages.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch MED 17.7.3.1 (A highly advanced, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system utilizing fast-acting piezoelectric injectors. The engine-driven twin High-Pressure Fuel Pumps (HPFP) inject fuel directly into the combustion chamber. Because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M276 suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract, requiring physical walnut blasting. Furthermore, European facelift models are equipped with restrictive Gasoline Particulate Filters (GPF/OPF) to meet Euro 6d-TEMP emissions.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum 3.0L BiTurbo M276 block is a masterpiece of engineering. It features NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating which practically eliminates piston friction and wear. Its lifespan in the W205 facelift chassis is exceptional if maintained correctly. The direct injection system naturally dilutes the engine oil with microscopic amounts of gasoline, meaning extending oil changes past 10 000 km will cause catastrophic bearing wear. If the cooling system is maintained and the oil changed religiously, the core engine is virtually bulletproof.)",
    turboType: "Twin-Turbocharged (Equipped with two advanced, fast-spooling IHI turbochargers, one mounted directly to each cylinder bank. For the facelift 390hp version, AMG increased the size of the turbochargers slightly and raised factory boost pressure to 1.1 bar. This setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, delivering 520 Nm of torque. They are highly reliable, though vacuum lines controlling the wastegates can crack from the intense engine bay heat generated by the GPFs.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.3.1 (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to tightly control the dual turbos and piezoelectric direct injection. The ECU actively monitors rail pressure, manages the electronic thermostat, controls the AMG Performance 4MATIC system, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port, unlocking true supercar performance.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with GPF/OPF in Europe)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.0-liter BiTurbo M276 is incredibly advanced and vastly overbuilt. The stock internals handle the 390hp rating effortlessly. The engine can easily be tuned to over 430 horsepower with just a software flash. Pushing past 450hp safely requires removing the highly restrictive GPF exhaust filters (where legal) and upgrading downpipes to manage the massive EGTs.)",
