    oilSpecification: "9.0L 5W-40 Low-SAPS Synthetic (MB 229.51 or 229.52 STRICTLY required due to the GPF/OPF exhaust filters. Using standard AMG 229.5 oil will destroy the filters. Checking the dipstick weekly is mandatory.)",
    commonIssues: [
      "Rear Main Seal (RMS) Failure: The absolute most notorious M177 issue. The PCV oil separators become clogged, pressurizing the crankcase and blowing out the rear main seal. This dumps massive amounts of engine oil and requires dropping the transmission to fix.",
      "GPF / OPF Sensor Failures: Facelift models feature restrictive Gasoline Particulate Filters. The differential pressure sensors frequently fail due to the massive V8 exhaust heat, triggering Check Engine lights and Limp Mode.",
      "Dynamic Engine Mount Failure: Exclusive to the C63 S, these electronically controlled fluid-filled mounts firm up during hard cornering. They frequently fail, leaking fluid and throwing a suspension malfunction code on the dashboard. They are astronomically expensive to replace.",
      "Ignition Coil Heat Death: The extreme heat generated by the 'Hot-V' turbochargers literally bakes the ignition coils over time. Under heavy boost, aging coils will misfire violently, triggering Limp Mode.",
      "AMG Performance Exhaust Valve Rattle: The electronic actuator flaps inside the AMG performance exhaust bind or rattle loudly over time due to soot and heat. Requires actuator replacement or exhaust modification.",
      "Twin High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The twin mechanical fuel pumps can wear internally, sending raw gasoline directly into the engine oil and destroying its lubricity."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Economic Total Loss (RMS & PCV Failure): If the RMS blows due to a clogged PCV system, the engine dumps oil rapidly. If driven without oil, the engine is destroyed. Even caught early, the repair requires removing the exhaust, transmission, and subframe, costing over 3,000 EUR.",
      "Exhaust Choking (GPF/OPF Clogging): European facelift models feature highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filters. If driven exclusively in city traffic or if incorrect non-Low-SAPS oil is used, the filter will permanently clog, forcing Limp Mode and requiring an immensely expensive replacement.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Fuel Dilution): If the High-Pressure Fuel Pumps leak internally, the gasoline-thinned oil will rapidly lose its lubricating properties. This fails to protect the main and rod bearings, causing the hand-built AMG engine to completely seize.",
      "Transmission Destruction (MCT Neglect): The new 9-speed MCT transmission is subjected to brutal 700 Nm shock-loads. Neglecting the strict 60,000 km fluid service will burn up the internal wet clutch pack, requiring a massive transmission rebuild.",
      "Heat Soak (Hot-V Turbos): The incredibly hot turbos in the engine valley will heat soak the intercoolers during repeated hard pulls, causing the ECU to drastically pull timing and cut horsepower to save the engine.",
      "Electronic Differential Destruction: The C 63 S uses a highly advanced electronic locking rear diff. If the fluid is not changed strictly (especially after the 3,000 km break-in period), the clutch packs will burn out, destroying the unit."
    ],
