    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM654 is an entirely new, pure Mercedes-Benz engine design, ditching the Renault roots of the pre-facelift. It utilizes a highly robust timing chain system located at the gearbox side. While significantly more durable than the older OM626, because the chain is located at the absolute rear, any required timing service involves complete engine or transmission removal. Frequent, high-quality oil changes are strictly required to maintain chain tensioner health.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 050 bar. It utilizes extremely precise solenoid injectors. To meet the ultra-strict Euro 6d-TEMP regulations, the exhaust is fitted with a highly complex aftertreatment system: a close-coupled Diesel Oxidation Catalyst (DOC), a Diesel Particulate Filter with SCR coating (sDPF), an SCR catalyst, and an AdBlue (DEF) injection system. This system is incredibly sensitive and prone to sensor failures.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The all-aluminum OM654 block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a masterpiece of diesel engineering. It is vastly superior and smoother than the outgoing Renault-based OM626. The core engine block is virtually indestructible. However, its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of its emissions systems. If driven exclusively in the city, the DPF and EGR will permanently clog, and the AdBlue system will fail, immobilizing the car. If driven strictly on the highway, it will run forever.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering 300 Nm of torque incredibly early. Because this specific C 180 d variant is aggressively software-restricted to just 122 horsepower, the turbocharger operates incredibly far below its thermal and mechanical limits, ensuring extreme longevity.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the 2050 bar injection, VGT turbo, and the incredibly complex multi-stage AdBlue and DPF regeneration cycles. Because this 1.6L block is mechanically capable of much more, the 122hp mapping is entirely artificial for tax purposes. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port, safely unlocking massive power.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with DPF, SCR, and AdBlue)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "190+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM654 is vastly overbuilt. Because it is artificially restricted to 122hp, the stock internals experience absolutely zero mechanical stress. A simple software flash easily pushes the engine to 170+ horsepower, completely transforming the lethargic C 180 d into a highly capable, fast commuter without stressing the bottom end.)",
