      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: Early OM654 engines can suffer from excessive wear on the roller rocker arms operating the valves. This leads to a distinct ticking noise from the top of the engine and eventual camshaft damage.",
      "EGR & DPF Clogging: The EGR system pumps massive amounts of soot back into the intake. If driven in the city, the DPF will choke, forcing the car into Limp Mode and requiring expensive forced regenerations.",
