    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM626 is essentially a heavily modified Renault R9M 1.6 dCi engine. It utilizes a simplex (single-row) timing chain. While generally reliable in lighter Renault models, the heavy W205 chassis puts extra strain on this small engine. The timing chain is known to stretch over high mileages (150,000+ km), causing a distinct cold-start metallic rattle. If ignored, the chain will snap or jump teeth. Preventative replacement is necessary if the rattle develops.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17 (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system. While reliable, the fuel injectors are highly sensitive to poor fuel quality. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are notoriously problematic on this Renault-derived engine, especially if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Renault R9M/OM626 is robust. However, its lifespan in the heavy C-Class is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to address complex emission system failures. The EGR valve, DPF, and the exhaust backpressure sensors fail frequently. Furthermore, this engine is known for oil leaks around the timing chain cover and the oil cooler. If the emissions systems are kept clean and the timing chain is replaced when it rattles, the engine will survive long autobahn commutes.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering 300 Nm of torque early. However, the VGT mechanism is highly prone to clogging with soot from the EGR system, causing the turbo to bind and throwing the car into a severe underboost Limp Mode.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the injection, VGT turbo, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. Tuning potential is excellent via the OBD-II port, safely unlocking significant power without stressing the internals.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "160+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM626 is quite strong for its size. The stock internals are vastly overbuilt for this 136hp output. A simple software flash easily pushes the engine past 160 horsepower, completely transforming the C 200 d into a very capable commuter.)",
