    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 utilizes a notorious simplex timing chain positioned against the firewall. Over high mileages (200,000+ km) or with extended oil change intervals, the chain stretches and the hydraulic tensioner fails. This causes a distinct, loud 3-5 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the chain skips teeth, destroying the engine. Because it is located at the rear, replacing the chain requires dropping the transmission or removing the entire engine, making the labor astronomically expensive.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 000 bar. The OM651 uses incredibly sensitive piezoelectric injectors. They are notorious for failing, causing severe misfires, rough idling, and white smoke. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are highly problematic if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Mercedes OM651 is legendary for its durability. However, its lifespan is entirely dictated by the terrifyingly expensive rear timing chain and injector failures. Furthermore, the plastic fuel filter housing/water neck assembly cracks, causing sudden, catastrophic coolant leaks. This specific ECO variant features aerodynamic and gearing changes, but the core engine flaws remain identical. If the chain is replaced preventatively, the injectors monitored, and the emissions systems kept clean, the engine block itself is virtually indestructible.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a robust Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering a massive 360 Nm of torque incredibly early. Because this 2.1L engine is restricted to just 136hp, the turbocharger operates incredibly far below its thermal and mechanical limits, ensuring extreme longevity unless starved of oil.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD3 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the sensitive piezo injectors, VGT turbo, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. This specific OM651.911 ECO variant has specialized ECU mapping to maximize fuel efficiency alongside its taller gearing. However, because the block is mechanically identical to the 170hp C 220 d, tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6 (Factory DPF & BlueTEC/AdBlue Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. Because it is artificially restricted to 136hp, the stock internals experience absolutely zero mechanical stress. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the engine to 170-200 horsepower. Note: Because the ECO version has taller gearing, acceleration will still feel slightly different than a standard C 200 d even after tuning.)",
