      "Overheating (Coolant Dump): If the plastic coolant housing cracks completely, the engine will lose all coolant in seconds, warping the cylinder head.",
      "Immobilization (AdBlue System Failure): A failed NOx sensor or AdBlue heater triggers a countdown that will eventually permanently refuse to start the engine.",
      "Limp Mode (Swirl Flaps/DPF): Broken swirl flaps or a clogged DPF will instantly throw the car into a highly restrictive Limp Mode.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (7G-Tronic Neglect): The 722.9 7-speed transmission requires strict fluid changes every 60 000 km to prevent conductor plate failure."
