      "Exhaust Choking (DPF Failure): If the car is exclusively driven in stop-and-go city traffic, the DPF will permanently clog. The ECU will cut power, and a replacement DPF costs over 2,000 EUR due to the integrated SCR coating.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Rocker Arm Failure): If the ticking noise from the top of the cylinder head is ignored, the worn rocker arms will destroy the camshaft lobes, requiring a massive engine rebuild.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (9G-Tronic Neglect): The 725.0 9-speed transmission requires incredibly strict fluid changes at 90 000 km using specialized gold ATF and a new integrated plastic pan.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Timing Chain): The chain is robust, but located at the back of the engine. If poor oil maintenance causes the tensioner to fail and the chain to snap, the engine is destroyed, and repair requires engine removal."
