      "Coolant Leak (Fuel Filter Housing): The plastic water neck/fuel filter housing on the side of the engine cracks from heat cycles, dumping coolant rapidly and causing sudden overheating.",
      "Intake Manifold Swirl Flaps: The plastic swirl flaps inside the intake manifold bind with soot and snap. The actuator arm breaks, throwing the car into Limp Mode.",
      "EGR & DPF Clogging: The EGR pumps soot into the intake. City driving guarantees the DPF will choke, forcing Limp Mode."
