    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 050 bar. It utilizes extremely precise solenoid injectors. To meet the ultra-strict Euro 6d-TEMP regulations, the exhaust is fitted with a highly complex aftertreatment system: a close-coupled Diesel Oxidation Catalyst (DOC), a Diesel Particulate Filter with SCR coating (sDPF), an SCR catalyst, and an AdBlue injection system. This system is incredibly sensitive and prone to sensor failures.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654 block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a legendary piece of diesel engineering. The core engine block is virtually indestructible. However, its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of its emissions systems. If driven exclusively in the city, the DPF and EGR will permanently clog, and the AdBlue system will fail, immobilizing the car. If driven strictly on the highway, it will easily surpass half a million kilometers.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering 400 Nm of torque incredibly early. The turbocharger operates comfortably within its efficiency range, ensuring extreme longevity if the oil is maintained.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the 2050 bar injection, VGT turbo, and the incredibly complex multi-stage AdBlue and DPF regeneration cycles. Tuning potential is absolutely staggering via the OBD-II port, safely unlocking massive power.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with DPF, SCR, and AdBlue)",
