    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 utilizes a notorious simplex timing chain positioned against the firewall. Over high mileages (200,000+ km) or with extended oil change intervals, the chain stretches and the hydraulic tensioner fails. This causes a distinct, loud 3-5 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the chain skips teeth, destroying the engine. Because it is located at the rear, replacing the chain requires dropping the transmission or removing the entire engine, making the labor astronomically expensive.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 000 bar. The OM651 uses incredibly sensitive piezoelectric injectors. They are notorious for failing, causing severe misfires, rough idling, and white smoke. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are problematic if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "350 000 - 600 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Mercedes OM651 is legendary for its durability. This specific early Euro 5 variant is HIGHLY SOUGHT AFTER because it completely lacks the fragile, failure-prone AdBlue (SCR) system found on later Euro 6 BlueTEC models. This removes the greatest immobilization risk from the car entirely. However, its lifespan is still dictated by the terrifyingly expensive rear timing chain and injector failures. If the chain is replaced preventatively and the injectors monitored, this is arguably the most reliable diesel W205 available.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a robust Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering a massive 400 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. The turbocharger is generally highly reliable, provided the engine receives regular, high-quality oil changes to protect the bearings.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD3 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the sensitive piezo injectors, VGT turbo, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. Crucially, because this is a Euro 5 engine, the ECU is NOT burdened with monitoring an AdBlue system. Tuning potential is absolutely phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5 (Factory DPF Equipped / NO ADBLUE)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "240+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. Designed to handle over 500 Nm of torque in higher-tier twin-turbo models, the stock internals handle the 170hp rating effortlessly. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the engine to 210-220 horsepower, making it a very fast, efficient cruiser.)",
