    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 utilizes a notorious simplex timing chain positioned against the firewall. Over high mileages (200,000+ km) or with extended oil change intervals, the chain stretches and the hydraulic tensioner fails. This causes a distinct, loud 3-5 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the chain skips teeth, destroying the engine. Because it is located at the rear, replacing the chain requires dropping the transmission or removing the entire engine, making the labor astronomically expensive.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 000 bar. The OM651 in the W205 uses incredibly sensitive piezoelectric injectors. They are notorious for failing, causing severe misfires, rough idling, and white smoke. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are highly problematic if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Mercedes OM651 is legendary for its durability, frequently surpassing half a million kilometers in taxi service. However, its lifespan for private owners is entirely dictated by the terrifyingly expensive rear timing chain and injector failures. Furthermore, the plastic fuel filter housing/water neck assembly cracks, causing sudden, catastrophic coolant leaks. If the chain is replaced preventatively, the injectors monitored, and the emissions systems kept clean, the engine block itself is virtually indestructible.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a robust Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, delivering a massive 400 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. The turbocharger is generally highly reliable, provided the engine receives regular, high-quality oil changes to protect the bearings.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD3 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the sensitive piezo injectors, VGT turbo, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. This specific OM651.911 variant is the absolute most common Euro 6 engine, heavily burdened with monitoring the complex AdBlue (SCR) injection system via delicate NOx sensors. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6 (Factory DPF & BlueTEC/AdBlue Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "240+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. Designed to handle over 500 Nm of torque in higher-tier twin-turbo models, the stock internals handle the 170hp rating effortlessly. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the engine to 210-220 horsepower, making it a very fast, efficient cruiser.)",
