    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 utilizes a notorious simplex timing chain positioned against the firewall. Over high mileages (200,000+ km) or with extended oil change intervals, the chain stretches and the hydraulic tensioner fails. This causes a distinct, loud 3-5 second metallic rattle on cold starts. If ignored, the chain skips teeth, destroying the engine. Because it is located at the rear, replacing the chain requires dropping the transmission or removing the entire engine, making the labor astronomically expensive.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 000 bar. The OM651 uses incredibly sensitive piezoelectric injectors. They are notorious for failing, causing severe misfires, rough idling, and white smoke. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are highly problematic if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Mercedes OM651 is legendary for its durability. This 204hp variant pushes the highest factory output for the 2.1L block, placing more stress on the internals, but the block handles it easily. However, its lifespan is entirely dictated by the terrifyingly expensive rear timing chain and injector failures. Furthermore, the plastic fuel filter housing/water neck assembly cracks, causing sudden, catastrophic coolant leaks. If the chain is replaced preventatively, the injectors monitored, and the emissions systems kept clean, the engine block itself is virtually indestructible.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Unlike the single-turbo C 220 d, the C 250 d is equipped with a sophisticated sequential two-stage turbo setup. A small high-pressure turbocharger provides instant response at low RPMs, seamlessly transitioning to a larger low-pressure turbocharger at higher RPMs. This delivers a massive 500 Nm of torque almost instantly and sustains power to the redline. Highly robust, but the complex vacuum actuation system can fail.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD3 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the sensitive piezo injectors, the sequential twin turbos, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. The European BlueTEC models also feature a complex AdBlue injection system that the ECU must constantly monitor via delicate NOx sensors. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6 (BlueTEC / AdBlue Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. Designed to handle over 500 Nm of torque natively, the stock internals are highly durable. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the twin-turbo engine to 240-250 horsepower and nearly 600 Nm of torque, making it a seriously fast diesel sedan.)",
