      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Timing Chain Snapping): If the rear timing chain snaps or skips teeth due to a failed tensioner, pistons will smash into the valves. Complete engine destruction.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Injector Failure): If a piezo injector fails and sticks open, it will wash the cylinder wall of oil or melt a hole straight through the piston.",
      "Overheating (Coolant Dump): If the plastic coolant housing cracks completely, the engine will lose all coolant in seconds, warping the cylinder head.",
      "Limp Mode (Sequential Turbo Failure): Vacuum leaks in the twin-turbo control system will instantly throw the car into a highly restrictive Limp Mode.",
