    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM654 utilizes a highly robust timing chain system located at the gearbox side. While significantly more durable than the older OM651, because the chain is located at the absolute rear, any required timing service involves complete engine or transmission removal. Frequent, high-quality oil changes are strictly required to maintain chain tensioner health.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 050 bar. It utilizes extremely precise solenoid injectors. To meet the ultra-strict Euro 6d-TEMP regulations, the exhaust is fitted with a highly complex aftertreatment system: a close-coupled Diesel Oxidation Catalyst (DOC), a Diesel Particulate Filter with SCR coating (sDPF), an SCR catalyst, and an AdBlue injection system. This system is incredibly sensitive and prone to sensor failures.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654 block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a legendary piece of diesel engineering. The core engine block is virtually indestructible, even in this high-output 245hp variant. However, its lifespan in the W205 chassis is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of its emissions systems. If driven exclusively in the city, the DPF and EGR will permanently clog, and the AdBlue system will fail, immobilizing the car. If driven strictly on the highway, it will easily surpass half a million kilometers.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (Unlike the single-turbo C 220 d, the C 300 d features a sophisticated sequential twin-turbo setup. A small high-pressure turbocharger provides instantaneous response off the line, seamlessly transitioning to a larger low-pressure turbocharger at higher RPMs. This setup entirely eliminates turbo lag, delivering a massive 500 Nm of torque incredibly early and sustaining 245hp to the redline.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the 2050 bar injection, the complex sequential twin turbos, and the incredibly complex multi-stage AdBlue and DPF regeneration cycles. Because this engine natively produces 245hp, it is already highly optimized, but tuning potential remains excellent via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP (Equipped with DPF, SCR, and AdBlue)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0L OM654 is vastly overbuilt. Even at 245hp, the stock internals experience little mechanical stress. A simple Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the sequential twin-turbo engine past 280 horsepower and nearly 600 Nm of torque, transforming the car into an absolute autobahn missile.)",
    fuelConsumption: {
      city: "6.5 - 7.5 L/100km",
      highway: "4.8 - 5.8 L/100km",
      mixed: "5.5 - 6.5 L/100km",
      sporty: "8.5+ L/100km"
    },
    oilSpecification: "6.0L 5W-30 Low-SAPS Synthetic (MB 229.52 STRICTLY REQUIRED to prevent immediate DPF and SCR catalyst poisoning.)",
    commonIssues: [
      "AdBlue (SCR) System Failures: THE absolute defining nightmare of Euro 6d-TEMP diesels. The NOx sensors, the AdBlue heater element, or the AdBlue pump module frequently fail. This triggers a Check Engine light and an inescapable 'Starts Remaining' countdown on the dashboard.",
      "Sequential Turbo Vacuum Issues: The complex vacuum lines and actuators controlling the transition between the small and large turbochargers often leak or fail, causing severe flat spots in acceleration.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: Early OM654 engines can suffer from excessive wear on the roller rocker arms operating the valves. This leads to a distinct ticking noise from the top of the engine and eventual camshaft damage.",
      "EGR & DPF Clogging: The EGR system pumps massive amounts of soot back into the intake. If driven in the city, the DPF will choke, forcing the car into Limp Mode and requiring expensive forced regenerations.",
      "9G-Tronic Conductor Plate: The highly advanced 9-speed transmission is brilliant but sensitive. It requires incredibly strict fluid changes using specialized gold fluid. Neglect causes harsh shifting and Limp Mode."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Immobilization (AdBlue Countdown): If ANY component of the AdBlue system fails (sensor, pump, heater), the ECU will initiate a strict countdown. Once the countdown reaches zero, the car is permanently immobilized and will refuse to start until the hugely expensive repair is completed.",
      "Limp Mode (Sequential Turbo Failure): Vacuum leaks in the twin-turbo control system will instantly throw the car into a highly restrictive Limp Mode, severely crippling performance.",
      "Exhaust Choking (DPF Failure): If the car is exclusively driven in stop-and-go city traffic, the DPF will permanently clog. The ECU will cut power, and a replacement DPF costs over 2,000 EUR due to the integrated SCR coating.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Rocker Arm Failure): If the ticking noise from the top of the cylinder head is ignored, the worn rocker arms will destroy the camshaft lobes, requiring a massive engine rebuild.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (9G-Tronic Neglect): The 725.0 9-speed transmission requires incredibly strict fluid changes at 90 000 km using specialized gold ATF and a new integrated plastic pan."
    ],
