    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 utilizes a notorious simplex timing chain positioned against the firewall. Over high mileages (200,000+ km) or with extended oil change intervals, the chain stretches and the hydraulic tensioner fails. This causes a distinct, loud 3-5 second metallic rattle on cold starts. In a hybrid application where the engine constantly turns on and off while driving, this wear is severely accelerated. Preventative replacement of the chain is critical.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Delphi (A high-pressure common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 000 bar. The OM651 uses incredibly sensitive piezoelectric injectors. They are notorious for failing, causing severe misfires, rough idling, and white smoke. Furthermore, the exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) valve and the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) are highly problematic if the car is driven primarily in stop-and-go city traffic, leading to massive soot clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 400 000+ km (The core cast-iron block of the Mercedes OM651 is legendary for its durability. However, its lifespan in the C 300 h is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of the parallel hybrid system. The internal combustion engine is frequently turned on and off violently while driving, meaning it is often subjected to high loads while completely cold. This massive thermal shock accelerates wear on the head gasket, turbochargers, and rear timing chain. Furthermore, the high-voltage hybrid battery degrades over time, and its replacement cost is staggering.)",
    turboType: "Sequential Twin-Turbocharged (The C 300 h utilizes the incredibly potent 204hp OM651 engine equipped with a sophisticated sequential two-stage turbo setup. A small high-pressure turbocharger provides instant response at low RPMs, seamlessly transitioning to a larger low-pressure turbocharger at higher RPMs. When combined with the electric motor's 250 Nm of instant torque, the acceleration is violently fast off the line. Highly robust, but the complex vacuum actuation system can fail.)",
    ecuType: "Delphi CRD3 (A sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the sensitive piezo injectors, the sequential twin turbos, EGR, and DPF regeneration cycles. It must also seamlessly integrate the 204hp combustion engine with the 27hp electric motor sandwiched inside the transmission. The European BlueTEC models also feature a complex AdBlue injection system. Tuning potential is phenomenal but highly complex due to the hybrid integration.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6 (BlueTEC / AdBlue Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp (Combustion Engine Only) (The internal rotating assembly of the OM651 is vastly overbuilt. However, pushing the combustion engine further via tuning is incredibly risky on the C 300 h, as the 7-speed transmission is already dealing with massive combined system torque from the twin turbos and the electric motor. Pushing past this limit will rapidly destroy the transmission clutch packs.)",
