      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: THE defining flaw of the OM651. The simplex chain stretches, causing a loud cold-start rattle. This is severely exacerbated by the engine constantly starting and stopping while driving.",
      "AdBlue (NOx Sensor) Failure: Standard European BlueTEC models suffer from constant NOx sensor and AdBlue heater failures, triggering a 'Starts Remaining' countdown that eventually permanently immobilizes the car.",
      "Delphi Piezo Injector Failure: The sensitive injectors fail internally, causing rough idling, massive power loss, white smoke, or even piston melting if stuck open.",
      "Coolant Leak (Fuel Filter Housing): The plastic water neck/fuel filter housing on the side of the engine cracks from heat cycles, dumping coolant rapidly and causing sudden overheating."
