    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC17 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 050 bar. To meet the ultra-strict Euro 6d-TEMP regulations, the exhaust is fitted with a highly complex aftertreatment system: a close-coupled Diesel Oxidation Catalyst (DOC), a Diesel Particulate Filter with SCR coating (sDPF), an SCR catalyst, and an AdBlue injection system. This system is incredibly sensitive and prone to sensor failures.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654 block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a legendary piece of diesel engineering. However, its lifespan in the C 300 de is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of the Plug-in Hybrid system. The engine operates under severe, unique stresses: the internal combustion engine is frequently turned on and off violently while driving, meaning it is often subjected to full load while completely cold. Furthermore, the 13.5 kWh high-voltage battery degrades over time, and its replacement cost often exceeds the value of the car.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The physical turbo is identical to the C 220 d, but in this PHEV application, the massive instant torque from the electric motor completely masks any turbo lag. The turbocharger operates comfortably within its efficiency range, ensuring extreme longevity if the oil is maintained.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC17 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the 2050 bar injection, VGT turbo, and the incredibly complex multi-stage AdBlue and DPF regeneration cycles. It must also seamlessly integrate the 194hp combustion engine with the 122hp electric motor sandwiched inside the transmission. Tuning potential is phenomenal but highly complex due to the hybrid integration.)",
