    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch (A state-of-the-art, ultra-high-pressure gasoline direct injection system. The engine-driven High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) injects fuel directly into the combustion chamber. Because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M264 suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract over time. Furthermore, all European models are equipped with a Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF/OPF).)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ km (The all-aluminum 1.5L M264 block features advanced CONICSHAPE cylinder honing and is mechanically incredibly robust. However, its lifespan in the W206 chassis is entirely dictated by the 48V EQ Boost mild-hybrid system. Unlike the later M254's transmission-mounted ISG, this M264 uses a Belt-driven Starter-Generator (BSG). If the 48V battery, inverter, or the BSG fails, the car is immobilized.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced, fast-spooling twin-scroll exhaust gas turbocharger. This twin-scroll setup entirely eliminates traditional turbo lag, working in tandem with the 48V belt-driven electric motor to provide seamless, instantaneous torque off the line before the turbo fully spools.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, highly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the combustion engine with the 48V BSG EQ Boost system. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery, manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM (Equipped with GPF/OPF)",
