    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch (A state-of-the-art gasoline direct injection system operating at incredible pressures. Because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M254 suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract over time. Furthermore, all European models are equipped with a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter / GPF to meet Euro 6d-ISC-FCM emissions.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L M254 block features advanced NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating and CONICSHAPE honing. Mechanically, the core engine is incredibly robust and easily handles the 258hp output. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the 48V Integrated Starter-Generator (ISG) system. The W206 uses a Gen-2 ISG sandwiched between the engine and transmission. If this hybrid motor or its high-voltage inverter fails, the repair requires dropping the transmission and costs astronomical amounts.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced twin-scroll turbocharger developed with Mercedes-AMG F1 technology. It features an electrified wastegate and works in perfect tandem with the 200 Nm EQ Boost from the ISG to entirely eliminate traditional turbo lag, delivering a highly authoritative and responsive powerband.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, incredibly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the combustion engine with the 48V Gen-2 ISG. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery, manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure. Tuning is highly complex due to the hybrid torque-fill integration.)",
