    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The brand new M254 engine moved the timing chain to the gearbox side to optimize pedestrian safety and front-end packaging. While highly robust and heavily revised from the older M264, replacing a stretched chain requires completely removing the engine or dropping the transmission. Strict oil changes are mandatory to protect the hydraulic tensioner.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch (A state-of-the-art gasoline direct injection system operating at incredible pressures. Because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M254 suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract over time. Crucially, the US Market model does NOT feature the highly restrictive Gasoline Particulate Filter / GPF found on European models, making it significantly less prone to exhaust clogging.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ miles (The all-aluminum 2.0L M254 block features advanced NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating and CONICSHAPE honing. Mechanically, the core engine is incredibly robust and easily handles the 255hp output. However, the lifespan is entirely dictated by the 48V Integrated Starter-Generator (ISG) system. The W206 uses a Gen-2 ISG sandwiched between the engine and transmission. If this hybrid motor or its high-voltage inverter fails, the repair requires dropping the transmission and costs astronomical amounts.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced twin-scroll turbocharger developed with Mercedes-AMG F1 technology. It features an electrified wastegate and works in perfect tandem with the 200 Nm EQ Boost from the ISG to entirely eliminate traditional turbo lag, delivering a highly authoritative and responsive powerband tailored for US highway merging.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, incredibly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the combustion engine with the 48V Gen-2 ISG. The ECU actively monitors the high-voltage battery and manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift. Tuning is highly complex due to the hybrid torque-fill integration, but the lack of a GPF allows for more aggressive timing.)",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 3 (NO GPF / OPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M254 is incredibly robust. The stock internals experience very little mechanical stress at 255hp. Because the US market lacks the highly restrictive GPF exhaust filter, the turbocharger breathes significantly better, making tuning far easier and more rewarding than on European variants.)",
