    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The brand new M254 engine moved the timing chain to the gearbox side. In this PHEV application, the engine constantly turns on and off while driving, subjecting the timing chain and tensioner to severe, accelerated wear. Replacing a stretched chain requires completely removing the engine or dropping the transmission. Strict 10,000 km oil changes are mandatory.)",
    injectionType: "Direct Injection / Bosch (A state-of-the-art gasoline direct injection system operating at incredible pressures. Because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M254 suffers from performance-robbing carbon buildup on the intake tract. Furthermore, all European models are equipped with a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter / GPF to meet Euro 6d-ISC-FCM emissions.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L M254 block is incredibly robust. However, its lifespan in the C 300 e is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of the Plug-in Hybrid system. The engine operates under severe, unique stresses: the internal combustion engine is frequently turned on and off violently while driving, meaning it is often subjected to full load while completely cold. This massive thermal shock accelerates wear on the head gasket and turbocharger. Furthermore, the massive 25.4 kWh high-voltage battery degrades over time, and its replacement cost is astronomical.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced twin-scroll turbocharger. The physical turbo is highly efficient, but in this PHEV application, the massive 440 Nm of instant torque from the electric motor completely masks any turbo lag. The turbo is subjected to intense thermal shock when the engine fires up suddenly at highway speeds.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (A lightning-fast, incredibly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the 204hp combustion engine with the powerful 129hp electric motor sandwiched inside the transmission. The ECU actively monitors the massive high-voltage battery, regenerative braking, manages the CAMTRONIC variable valve lift, and strictly monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure. Tuning is incredibly difficult.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM (Equipped with GPF/OPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (Combustion Engine Only) (The internal rotating assembly of the 2.0-liter M254 is vastly overbuilt. However, pushing the combustion engine further via tuning is incredibly risky on the C 300 e, as the 9-speed transmission is already dealing with a massive 550 Nm of combined system torque. Pushing past this limit risks destroying the transmission clutch packs.)",
