      "Economic Total Loss (High-Voltage Battery): If the massive 25.4 kWh hybrid battery completely fails out of warranty, the replacement cost (often 8 000 - 12 000 EUR) frequently exceeds the residual value of the car.",
      "Immobilization (Hybrid System Fault): A failure in the high-voltage wiring, inverter, or electric motor will trigger a red warning on the dashboard and permanently lock the drivetrain, requiring a tow to the dealership.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Cold Stress): Because the hybrid system frequently demands instant high power from a completely cold combustion engine, the head gasket and turbocharger are subjected to severe, accelerated thermal shock.",
      "Exhaust Choking (GPF/OPF Clogging): European models feature a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter. If driven exclusively in stop-and-go city traffic, or if incorrect non-Low-SAPS oil is used, the filter will permanently clog, forcing Limp Mode.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Fuel Dilution): If the High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) internal leak is ignored, the gasoline-thinned oil will rapidly lose its lubricating properties, destroying the main bearings and seizing the engine.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (9G-Tronic Hybrid Neglect): The 725.0 transmission must handle 550 Nm of torque AND house an electric motor. It requires incredibly strict fluid changes every 90 000 km using specialized gold fluid."
