    commonIssues: [
      "High-Voltage Battery Degradation: The W206 PHEV uses a massive 25.4 kWh lithium-ion battery. It loses capacity significantly over time. When it drops below a certain threshold, the pure EV range disappears, and replacing the battery module costs an astronomical amount.",
      "Hybrid System Component Failure: The power electronics, the electric motor sandwiched in the transmission, or the high-voltage charging module can fail. Any failure in the high-voltage loop instantly immobilizes the vehicle.",
      "GPF / OPF Sensor Failures: Features a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter. The differential pressure sensors frequently fail due to extreme heat, triggering Check Engine lights and Limp Mode.",
      "Thermostat & Thermal Management Failure: The incredibly complex electronic thermostat and heat management modules frequently fail, causing the engine to run cold or overheat rapidly.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Leaks: The mechanical fuel pump can leak internally, sending raw gasoline directly into the engine oil and destroying its lubricity."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Economic Total Loss (High-Voltage Battery): If the massive 25.4 kWh hybrid battery completely fails out of warranty, the replacement cost (often 8 000 - 12 000 EUR) frequently exceeds the residual value of the car.",
      "Immobilization (Hybrid System Fault): A failure in the high-voltage wiring, inverter, or electric motor will trigger a red warning on the dashboard and permanently lock the drivetrain, requiring a tow to the dealership.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Cold Stress): Because the hybrid system frequently demands instant high power from a completely cold combustion engine, the head gasket and turbocharger are subjected to severe, accelerated thermal shock.",
      "Exhaust Choking (GPF/OPF Clogging): European models feature a highly sensitive Gasoline Particulate Filter. If driven exclusively in stop-and-go city traffic, or if incorrect non-Low-SAPS oil is used, the filter will permanently clog, forcing Limp Mode.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Fuel Dilution): If the High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) internal leak is ignored, the gasoline-thinned oil will rapidly lose its lubricating properties, destroying the main bearings and seizing the engine.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (9G-Tronic Hybrid Neglect): The 725.0 transmission must handle massive system torque AND house an electric motor. It requires incredibly strict fluid changes every 90 000 km using specialized gold fluid."
    ],
