    injectionType: "Combined Direct and Port Injection / Bosch (A highly complex dual-injection system. It utilizes extremely high-pressure piezoelectric direct injectors alongside traditional manifold port injectors. This dual system provides massive fueling for 408hp while simultaneously keeping the intake valves completely clean of carbon buildup, a massive advantage over standard M254 engines. Features GPF/OPF exhaust filters.)",
    engineLifespan: "150 000 - 250 000+ km (The M139L is an engineering masterpiece. It features a closed-deck, chill-cast aluminum block capable of withstanding immense cylinder pressures, with NANOSLIDE coating and forged internals. Mechanically, the block is race-ready. However, its lifespan in the W206 is dictated entirely by its staggering complexity. The F1-derived electric turbocharger is highly prone to overheating and failure. Furthermore, the 48V ISG system adds a layer of failure points that will immobilize the car.)",
    turboType: "Electrically Assisted Exhaust Gas Turbocharger (Derived directly from Mercedes-AMG Petronas F1 technology. An incredibly advanced turbocharger with a tiny 48V electric motor integrated directly onto the turbo shaft between the compressor and turbine wheel. It spools the turbo electronically before exhaust gases take over, completely eliminating turbo lag. While brilliant, it runs incredibly hot and is highly prone to failure. Replacement is astronomically expensive.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (An ultra-fast, incredibly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the M139 block, the 48V ISG, and the revolutionary F1 electric turbocharger. The ECU actively monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure and aggressively pulls timing if the electric turbo overheats. Tuning is highly complex.)",
