    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The M139L is a longitudinally mounted, extensively modified version of the A45 AMG engine. Given the insane 476hp specific output from just 2.0 liters, strict 5,000 km oil changes are absolutely critical to protect the timing chain and the highly stressed hydraulic tensioners. Replacing a stretched chain requires dropping the transmission or removing the engine entirely.)",
    injectionType: "Combined Direct and Port Injection / Bosch (A highly complex dual-injection system. It utilizes extremely high-pressure piezoelectric direct injectors alongside traditional manifold port injectors. This dual system provides massive fueling for the 476hp 4-cylinder while simultaneously keeping the intake valves clean of carbon buildup. Features GPF/OPF exhaust filters.)",
    engineLifespan: "100 000 - 200 000+ km (The M139L block is a closed-deck, chill-cast masterpiece capable of withstanding immense cylinder pressures. However, its lifespan in the C 63 S is dictated entirely by its unfathomable complexity. This is arguably the most complex powertrain in production car history. It utilizes a highly stressed 4-cylinder engine, an F1-derived electric turbocharger, a 400V AMG High-Performance Battery, and a P3-layout rear-axle Electric Drive Unit (EDU) with its own 2-speed transmission. The points of failure are practically infinite. If any component in the high-voltage loop fails, the car is immobilized.)",
    turboType: "Electrically Assisted Exhaust Gas Turbocharger (Derived directly from Mercedes-AMG Petronas F1 technology. An incredibly advanced turbocharger with a 400V electric motor integrated directly onto the turbo shaft. It spools the turbo electronically before exhaust gases take over, completely eliminating turbo lag. It runs incredibly hot and is highly stressed pushing the 2.0L engine to 476hp.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch (An ultra-fast, incredibly complex engine management system designed to seamlessly integrate the M139 block, the 400V AMG High-Performance Battery, the rear-axle Electric Drive Unit (EDU), and the F1 electric turbocharger. The ECU actively monitors the GPF/OPF exhaust backpressure and orchestrates the massive 1020 Nm torque output. Tuning is nearly impossible due to the locked ECU and hybrid integration.)",
