    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch MD1 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 500 bar in the OM654M. To meet Euro 6d-ISC-FCM regulations, it features an incredibly complex dual-dosing SCR system: two SCR catalytic converters and twin AdBlue injectors, alongside a close-coupled DPF. Highly sensitive to fuel quality.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 400 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654M block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a masterpiece of diesel engineering. Mechanically, the core engine is virtually indestructible, especially in this massively detuned 136hp state. However, its lifespan in the W206 chassis is entirely dictated by the 48V ISG system and the dual-SCR emissions setup. If the transmission-mounted ISG or the complex AdBlue system fails, the repair costs are astronomical.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT) with a water-cooled bearing housing. The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, working in perfect tandem with the 200 Nm EQ Boost from the 48V electric motor to provide seamless off-the-line torque. In this 136hp application, the turbo operates effortlessly.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MD1 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the massive 2500 bar injection, VGT turbo, the 48V Gen-2 ISG torque fill, and the incredibly complex twin-dosing AdBlue regeneration cycles. Because this 2.0L block is mechanically capable of much more, the 136hp mapping is entirely artificial. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
