    timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM654M utilizes a highly robust timing chain system located at the gearbox side. While significantly more durable than the older OM651, replacing a stretched chain requires completely removing the engine or dropping the transmission. Strict 10,000 km oil changes are mandatory to maintain chain tensioner health and prevent catastrophic failure.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch MD1 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 500 bar in the OM654M. To meet Euro 6d-ISC-FCM regulations, it features an incredibly complex dual-dosing SCR system: two SCR catalytic converters and twin AdBlue injectors, alongside a close-coupled DPF. Highly sensitive to fuel quality.)",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 400 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654M block with NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating is a masterpiece of diesel engineering. Mechanically, the core engine is incredibly robust even at 265hp. However, its lifespan in the W206 chassis is entirely dictated by the 48V ISG system and the dual-SCR emissions setup. If the transmission-mounted ISG or the complex AdBlue system fails, the repair costs are astronomical.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT) with a water-cooled bearing housing. The variable vanes adjust exhaust flow to eliminate turbo lag, working in perfect tandem with the 200 Nm EQ Boost from the 48V electric motor to provide seamless off-the-line torque. In this 265hp application, the turbo operates at a much higher pressure.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MD1 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the massive 2500 bar injection, VGT turbo, the 48V Gen-2 ISG torque fill, and the incredibly complex twin-dosing AdBlue regeneration cycles. This represents the absolute pinnacle of 2.0L diesel mapping. Tuning potential is phenomenal via the OBD-II port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM (Equipped with DPF, Twin-SCR, and Dual AdBlue Injection)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the OM654M is vastly overbuilt. The stock internals handle the immense 265hp and 550Nm output effortlessly. A Stage 1 software flash safely pushes the engine to near 300 horsepower without stressing the bottom end, turning it into a true M340d rival.)",
    fuelConsumption: {
      city: "6.5 - 7.5 L/100km",
      highway: "4.5 - 5.5 L/100km",
      mixed: "5.5 - 6.5 L/100km",
      sporty: "8.5+ L/100km"
    },
    oilSpecification: "6.0L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Low-SAPS Synthetic (MB 229.71 or MB 229.52 STRICTLY REQUIRED to prevent immediate DPF and dual-SCR catalyst poisoning.)",
    commonIssues: [
      "Gen-2 ISG System Failure: The 48V Integrated Starter-Generator is sandwiched between the engine and gearbox. If the 48V battery, inverter, or the ISG itself fails, the car is completely immobilized. Replacing the ISG requires dropping the transmission.",
      "Dual AdBlue (SCR) System Failures: The W206 diesel features TWIN AdBlue injectors and TWO SCR catalysts. NOx sensor or AdBlue pump failures are extremely common and trigger an inescapable 'Starts Remaining' countdown on the dashboard.",
      "EGR & DPF Clogging: The EGR system pumps massive amounts of soot back into the intake. If driven in the city, the DPF will choke, forcing the car into Limp Mode.",
      "9G-Tronic Conductor Plate: The highly advanced 9-speed transmission is brilliant but sensitive. It requires incredibly strict fluid changes using specialized gold fluid.",
      "Water Pump Failure: The mechanical water pump features a vacuum-controlled plastic shroud designed to block coolant flow for faster warm-up. This shroud jams, causing rapid overheating."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Immobilization (48V ISG Failure): If the 48V battery or transmission-mounted ISG fails, the car is completely dead. The replacement requires advanced dealer-level diagnostics and dropping the 9-speed transmission, costing thousands of euros.",
      "Immobilization (AdBlue Countdown): If ANY component of the dual-dosing AdBlue system fails, the ECU will initiate a strict countdown. Once it reaches zero, the car is permanently immobilized.",
      "Exhaust Choking (DPF Failure): If the car is exclusively driven in stop-and-go city traffic, the DPF will permanently clog. The ECU will cut power, and a replacement DPF costs over 2,000 EUR.",
      "Transmission Limp Mode (9G-Tronic Neglect): The 725.0 9-speed transmission requires incredibly strict fluid changes at 90 000 km using specialized gold ATF and a new integrated plastic pan.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Damage (Rear Timing Chain): The chain is robust, but located at the back of the engine. If poor oil maintenance causes the tensioner to fail and the chain to snap, the engine is destroyed."
    ],
