    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch MD1 (A state-of-the-art, 4th generation common-rail diesel injection system operating at up to 2 500 bar. To meet Euro 6d-ISC-FCM regulations, it features an incredibly complex dual-dosing SCR system: two SCR catalytic converters and twin AdBlue injectors, alongside a close-coupled DPF. Highly sensitive to fuel quality.)",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The all-aluminum 2.0L OM654M block is incredibly robust. However, its lifespan in the C 300 de is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity of the Plug-in Hybrid system. The engine operates under severe, unique stresses: the internal combustion engine is frequently turned on and off violently while driving, meaning it is often subjected to full load while completely cold. This massive thermal shock accelerates wear on the head gasket and turbocharger. Furthermore, the massive 25.4 kWh high-voltage battery degrades over time, and its replacement cost is astronomical.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The physical turbo is highly efficient, but in this PHEV application, the massive 440 Nm of instant torque from the electric motor completely masks any turbo lag. The turbo is subjected to intense thermal shock when the engine fires up suddenly at highway speeds.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch MD1 (A highly sophisticated electronic diesel control module that manages the 2500 bar injection, VGT turbo, and the incredibly complex multi-stage AdBlue and DPF regeneration cycles. It must also seamlessly integrate the 197hp combustion engine with the powerful 129hp electric motor sandwiched inside the transmission. Tuning is incredibly difficult due to hybrid integration.)",
